game without DLC, Brujah, Assamites (Banu Haqim), Tremere, and Ventrue.<br /> <br /> All I can say is gross. Piecemealing content that should be core to the game is a terrible practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T16:33:22-07:00","id":1553271,"title":"","content":"This doesn't seem interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T16:37:49-07:00","id":1553274,"title":"","content":"At this point, just the fact that it will be released at all in October is a miracle. And I wouldn't hope for many DLCs at all after the first batch, it will greatly depend on the game's market performance, and it's not in the best place to do well.<br /> <br /> Not impossible, but it will be an uphill battle even if it's, in fact, good.<br /> <br /> Other than that, what can I say? The difference in play through will have a lot of weight into if this DLC approach is worth it or not for players. If it's like in the first game, then it's definitely BS, we should have at least 7 clans out of the bat. If it is a significantly bigger difference, though, it <i>may</i> be worth it.<br /> <br /> I'm not getting my hopes too high, though, especially given that we already know that the main character doesn't significantly change to begin with. Lets just see what October brings, without much expectation one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T20:00:57-07:00","id":1553276,"title":"","content":"It might not be complicated, but it's pretty common in the video-game industry right now: if you think your game is going to have a lot of day 1 purchases, but not have staying power, ramp up as much extra cash as you can in &quot;premium&quot; editions for early buyers.<br /> <br /> There's a reason that there's a massive &quot;no preorder&quot; campaign around Battlefield 6 despite the closed beta results being really positive: the company has a history and BF fans know that if they like the newest game, the best thing is to buy the base version and only pay extra for stuff over time so that Dice has to keep supporting the product if they want that DLC/microtransaction cash.&quot;<br /> <br /> Premium digital editions and massive price increases on games has fans being careful with their wallets. And fans are already growing more and more frustrated with how it's become standard practice in video games to constantly move things that used to be standard base features behind paywalls; and even good games coming out are hampered because if they plan on relying on microtransactions as part of their business model, there's ever growing data to show that gamers are sticking to games that have already gotten lots of money out of them. Why abandon a game you like and sunk $90 into already for a game you might like (even like just as much) when you're entering for $90 off the bat? <br /> <br /> Over the last few years we've seen dozens of games that people loved, but the player retention on them has been garbage. For games where you buy it, play it, and move on? That's fine. The company got the purchase. For games that are going to have future paid content? That doesn't work. If 95% of people that played your game are gone within a month, nobody is buying your future DLC.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> As for the new stuff specific to VtM... I really don't understand the marketing of &quot;hey, you get to play as the other perspective character too!&quot; as a major selling point in the new trailer (since that really does seem to be the only new thing). No customer cares about Phyre and Fabien yet because they're new characters made up for the game. Switching to a secondary protagonist for playing certain sections of a game has been around for decades... it's not some new fancy bit of game design people are going to be wowed by.<br /> <br /> I just don't see how this moves the needle for anybody (and the paid DLC for more Clans is going move it negatively.... was all the flak V5 took for making people pay extra for the full Clans not clear enough?). Anyone that pre-orders was going to do it regardless. Anyone that was on the fence hasn't been given any reason to put in money now instead of wait until November or December to see what actually players think of it (or longer for the many, many, many people that just wait for games to come around on sale if there's no compelling reason to jump in on day 1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T22:30:28-07:00","id":1553277,"title":"","content":"Guess i'll just stick to my &quot;digital tabletop&quot; V20 group of little weirdoes messing with bits of Redemption, OG Bloodlines &amp; BJD for a storyline then.<br /> <br /> Never wanted to be that old grump salty about the new generation of the game and how everything is a mess, but world is not helping....<br /> But considering half my players are 20 to 30-somethings, guess i'm not AS bad as that overall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T01:57:55-07:00","id":1553279,"title":"","content":"Man, they're really not making it easy to like this game... Day 1 DLC, paywalling Clan options and then it's a whopping 90 bucks, an extra 30 bucks?! That's insane!<br /> <br /> If somebody wants to read a preview, I'd recommend this article from Eurogamer called <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/more-action-than-rpg-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-struggles-to-convince-after-a-few-hours-play\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;More action than RPG, Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 struggles to convince after a few hours' play&quot;</a>. <br /> <br /> Reading that and looking at the trailers, my impression is that this game is 80% your typical walking-simulator, story-driven (although VERY linear) experience and then occasionally you will be put into these combat-arenas where you use your abilities and then there's some hub-world where you can use XP to buy additional abilities. Especially when this article mentions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nice though they are to look at, in these areas there's little you can actually interact with - a problem that carries right across the game. Take the city of Seattle, for instance, where the game's set. It looks nice, caught as it has been in heavy snowfall, and moody in the dark, lit by pools of streetlight or car headlights. But the only doors you can interact with are the ones that lead to specific quest objectives, of which there are only one or two in the preview build, and the only people you can interact with... Well, you can utter a few words to some people, in an effort to lead them into an alley to drink their blood, which regenerates health or regains special ability charges, or earns you a kind of upgrade currency, but that's about it. For the most part, it feels like a place filled with non-interactive extras. </div> </div> </div>Because of things like that and with that price-point in mind, my two biggest reservations right now are how long this game will end up being and how much true replay-value it has. Is there even a point in replaying this game with a different Clan (aside from maybe doing a more combat-focused run compared to a stealth-one)? Or even if the only difference is what sort of abilities you have, how does combat fare during playtime? What's the enemy-variety like, how interesting is the level-design of the places where you fight? Stuff like that. <br /> <br /> The impression I always had was that this was the type of game where an AA-type of price-tag (like 40 bucks for the base-game) will end up feeling more justified for what you will get out of the game. But to give it this quite hefty price-tag for its Premium Edition definitely ups the ante for what this game would have to present to convince me to buy it after launch at that price. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T02:50:29-07:00","id":1553280,"title":"","content":"This game is going to be an unbridled disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T03:20:18-07:00","id":1553281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/a0CbiNnaHcw\" data-code=\"a0CbiNnaHcw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/a0CbiNnaHcw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It looks...fine.<br /> <br /> I feel like this is a shocking statement but that's my impression. You're an Elder vampire with a Malkavian in their head (guessing the plot twist will be that you've been diablerized and overhelmed your attacker and are now in their body). You wake up after a 100 year torpor and proceed to beat the living shit out of whatever crisis is facing Seattle with probaly the option of getting to be the Prince at the end since that's not ridiculous if you're an Elder. It looks like it works like Dishonored but you have more punching and this will have a body count in the low hundreds. You will do lots of conversations and probably have sidequests which have three options.<br /> <br /> Which is fine.<br /> <br /> I'll probably enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Certainly more so than a lot of the V:TM games I've been playing.<br /> <br /> Will it be as awesome as Brian Mitsoda and Chris Avellone's Bloodlines? Probably not. Mitsoda would have certainly added a Tim Cain-esque authenticity to it. But it seems perfectly fun as a vampire game.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed Vampyre.<br /> <br /> Will it be worth the wait and delays? Absolutely not. But nothing could be at this point. Still, I don't forsee it being a Duke Nukem Forever or Cyberpunk 2077 at launch disaster either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T04:51:21-07:00","id":1553283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553281#post1553281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/a0CbiNnaHcw\" data-code=\"a0CbiNnaHcw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/a0CbiNnaHcw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It looks...fine.<br /> <br /> I feel like this is a shocking statement but that's my impression. You're an Elder vampire with a Malkavian in their head (guessing the plot twist will be that you've been diablerized and overhelmed your attacker and are now in their body). You wake up after a 100 year torpor and proceed to beat the living shit out of whatever crisis is facing Seattle with probaly the option of getting to be the Prince at the end since that's not ridiculous if you're an Elder. It looks like it works like Dishonored but you have more punching and this will have a body count in the low hundreds. You will do lots of conversations and probably have sidequests which have three options.<br /> <br /> Which is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of Swansong perhaps?<br /> Not a sucessor worthy of the original Bloodlines, but then doesn't mean you can't find a decent game below that high bar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553281#post1553281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll probably enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Certainly more so than a lot of the V:TM games I've been playing.<br /> <br /> Will it be as awesome as Brian Mitsoda and Chris Avellone's Bloodlines? Probably not. Mitsoda would have certainly added a Tim Cain-esque authenticity to it. But it seems perfectly fun as a vampire game.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed Vampyre.<br /> <br /> Will it be worth the wait and delays? Absolutely not. But nothing could be at this point. Still, I don't forsee it being a Duke Nukem Forever or Cyberpunk 2077 at launch disaster either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hardly anything would be worth - though one might say they lower general level of expectations more than anything so, nothing much to hope for either way?<br /> <br /> Probably better off doing our own things and checking on it in a year or whenever a finished game and reactions to it start pouring.<br /> <br /> Back to the &quot;Caitiff&quot; ex-Hound of prince Lacroix that discovered he's a modern Cappadocian, the Salubri warrior-nun, the so-called &quot;childe of Dracula&quot; with a magic sword, the &quot;de-gargoylized&quot; medieval Gangrel, the Caitiff DJ &quot;rogue&quot; childe of an archon and the Toreador noddist of good lineage with a Drowned Legacies obsession - and the Banu Haqim netcafe clerk anarch - to me...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T05:21:34-07:00","id":1553284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553277#post1553277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never wanted to be that old grump salty about the new generation of the game and how everything is a mess, but world is not helping....</div> </div> </div> </div>For whatever it's worth, I don't actually think the problem is the new generation. As far as I could see, most of the people behind the many messes from Paradox aren't that young or new to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553279#post1553279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, they're really not making it easy to like this game... Day 1 DLC, paywalling Clan options and then it's a whopping 90 bucks, an extra 30 bucks?! That's insane!<br /> <br /> If somebody wants to read a preview, I'd recommend this article from Eurogamer called <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/more-action-than-rpg-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-struggles-to-convince-after-a-few-hours-play\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;More action than RPG, Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 struggles to convince after a few hours' play&quot;</a>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For me it will be between R$ 450,00 and R$ 500,00, which is about half as expensive as it looks like. Quite prohibitive for most people, for something that really isn't that big of a deal, I have a long list of games I want more and cost less.<br /> <br /> I didn't read the preview because the site doesn't really let me reject cookies, even though it pretends it does, so that's a no deal. I'll take your word for it.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553280#post1553280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This game is going to be an unbridled disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think it may fare better than I expected not long ago.<br /> <br /> Which is still bad, it will be a miracle if they break even with it and I'll probably pass it until I get it at a discount, if ever.<br /> <br /> But in the full spectrum of how bad things could be, it now looks it will at least avoid the bottom.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553281#post1553281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks...fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> said. It doesn't look bad, but nothing in it indicates it'll be worth the price.<br /> <br /> We're looking at the price tag of an AAA, delivering less than the complete experience at the base game. The actual &quot;full&quot; game (if they didn't hide even more fundamental content behind &quot;future&quot; DLCs, which is a possibility) is as expensive as the most wanted games in the market right now.<br /> <br /> The graphics, for one, look underwhelming. I'm not just unimpressed with what I saw in this trailer, I'm effectively disappointed. Now, is this a deal breaker? Of course not. But for this type of game at this price tag, I'd expected cleaner results as a matter of course. Most of the time the characters managed to be less expressive than in the original Bloodlines, which isn't exactly the same thing as bad graphics but compounds the problem.<br /> <br /> It doesn't look terrible at all. After all that happened in this long wait, it has a real chance of being an ok game, although much remains to be seen. Nothing indicates it will be a transformative experience, but it has all the elements it needs for gameplay and level design alone making it good. And as far as I could see, it'll be a nice change of pace to have a VtM game that isn't just a glorified book, other than <i>Bloodhunt</i>.<br /> <br /> But all said and done, at this heft price tag it does seem they're just desperately trying to make as much as possible from the people that would buy at launch anyway, just to recover as much as possible from this sinkhole of money. It just isn't worth the price and they know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553281#post1553281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I don't forsee it being a Duke Nukem Forever or Cyberpunk 2077 at launch disaster either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't dismiss those possibilities so soon, depending on how you define them.<br /> <br /> What made DNF so badly received was a combination of unreal expectations and bad level design. It had other problems, but it was mostly bad level design. We don't have the unreal expectations at the same level, for several reasons, but the bad level design simply isn't out of question yet.<br /> <br /> C2077's launch was marred by bugs, and that's it. It had absolutely nothing to do with the game's actual quality in any other aspect. There <b>is</b> a criticism on its shallow portrayal of the Cyberpunk genre (which I think is actually in tune with the <i>Cyberpunk 2013</i> series, I've always been a critic of it), but the game was otherwise very well received. And the bugs weren't present in demo materials, so they mean nothing.<br /> <br /> Being riddled with bugs at launch is still something that can happen. Both types of disaster rely on things whose likelihood remains unchanged. It's low, by the way, but still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T05:37:50-07:00","id":1553285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553284#post1553284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For whatever it's worth, I don't actually think the problem is the new generation. As far as I could see, most of the people behind the many messes from Paradox aren't that young or new to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My &quot;grumpy old foggey&quot; comical routine - RUINED FOREVER!!!<br /> (Not like it was worth much as a joke anyways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Now back to Gargoyle &quot;civil war&quot;, Vukodlak x Zelios in Transylvanian Chronicles in America, Banu Haqim in Milwaukee and the Deadman's Party quest for Caine, among other shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T05:59:59-07:00","id":1553286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553284#post1553284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me it will be between R$ 450,00 and R$ 500,00, which is about half as expensive as it looks like. Quite prohibitive for most people, for something that really isn't that big of a deal, I have a long list of games I want more and cost less.<br /> <br /> I didn't read the preview because the site doesn't really let me reject cookies, even though it pretends it does, so that's a no deal. I'll take your word for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that cookie-policy they have over there isn't great...<br /> <br /> To at least get a sense of how the writer felt about the time he spent with the game, here are the conclusions at the end of the article:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look, there's still hope. This, it's worth remembering, is a preview build of a game still a couple of months from release, and it's only the start of the experience - the part that typically lays some ground rules before opening up and letting you do what you want to do. I fully expect this empty-feeling Seattle playground to populate with places to go and people to meet. At least, I hope that's the case. But I also expect a preview build to be designed to showcase the best parts of the game I'm previewing, and for the beginning of a game to grab and dazzle a player, and convince them to stick around. I did enjoy some of what I played, and I'm willing to give it another go. But I wasn't grabbed or dazzled.<br /> <br /> I'm always wary of critiquing a game for what it's not, rather than meeting it where it is - and just to emphasise, the focus on action here makes plenty of sense. But this is a sequel to a cult RPG after all, and one based on a major tabletop RPG to boot. In this case it feels valid to crave a little more role-playing, a little more texture and depth to the game's people and conversations. And so for now, a question mark remains.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I mean, these days, I think one should never pre-order a game. Period. Because you never know whether you get a game like Clair Obscur or at launch, you get a disaster like Cyberpunk 2077 and the game's barely playable. <br /> <br /> The game certainly now looks way better than the previews from a year ago. So clearly, the developers have been hard at work. But at this point, I would've loved to see more of the game. Anything really that would make me think &quot;I got to play this!&quot;. I'm not having this terrible feeling of it being an unfinished game like I did a year ago but aside from the combat, I'm not sold on any other aspect of the game right now. Because I've also got this fear about the scope of the game. All these supposedly exciting bits and pieces, they've only ever talked about in text in those various dev-blogs... Why, even at this stage, aren't they showing off those features? Like dialogue-choices impacting stuff beyond just the mood of the character that's talking with Phyre in the scene. Because, for example when the dev-blogs made a big deal about the &quot;social feeding&quot; when you're in the outer Seattle-hub-zone. That sounded somewhat interesting. But I feel deflated when I read in the preview that this guy's actual experience was just &quot;You go up to an NPC, press a button, a little bit of dialogue happens, the character automatically follows you into an alley, you drink from then - and that's that.&quot; And what if it's never more than that? That isn't outright bad - but it's also not exciting. Especially at that price-point. <br /> <br /> So if I have to choose between something uncertain like this, for example or simply wait for the release of Outer Worlds 2... right now, I'd rather pick the latter. Or (which would be the worst case scenario for Bloodlines 2, I feel like) it's announced Silksong will be coming out at the end of October. I'm definitely gonna play that one rather than Bloodlines 2 if that's the choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T08:26:12-07:00","id":1553288,"title":"","content":"Game press is starting to report on it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://kotaku.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-day-1-dlc-clans-2000618832\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://kotaku.com/app/uploads/2025/08/vampmasq-1200x675.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://kotaku.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-day-1-dlc-clans-2000618832\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloodlines 2 Locks Core Content Behind Costly Day-One DLC </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://kotaku.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-day-1-dlc-clans-2000618832\" target=\"_blank\"> https://kotaku.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-day-1-dlc-clans-2000618832 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> You'll need to pay half as much again to play the entire RPG when it launches </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-sticks-two-bloodsucker-clans-including-the-sexy-one-behind-paid-day-one-dlc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-two-clans-day-one-dlc-01.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;fit=crop&amp;enable=upscale&amp;auto=webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-sticks-two-bloodsucker-clans-including-the-sexy-one-behind-paid-day-one-dlc\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 sticks two bloodsucker clans, including the sexy one, behind paid day-one DLC </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-sticks-two-bloodsucker-clans-including-the-sexy-one-behind-paid-day-one-dlc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-sticks-two-bloodsucker-clans-including-the-sexy-one-behind-paid-day-one-dlc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Two of Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 clans, the Lasombra and Toreador, gated behind paid day-one DLC for the game. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T08:59:43-07:00","id":1553289,"title":"","content":"I guess, this is what in the biz you would call &quot;not a good look&quot;...<br /> <br /> Reading these articles, it's kinda astonishing how Paradox continues to suck as a publisher. I mean, think about this: Imagine if the reveal had simply been &quot;So far, we had talked about the game having four playable Clans. Guess what? It's actually six!&quot;. Imagine what the reaction would've been like if they had done that instead? But no, now the big talk about Bloodlines 2 is Day One DLC, paywalling essential content and corporate greed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T10:34:12-07:00","id":1553294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553286#post1553286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, these days, I think one should never pre-order a game. Period. Because you never know whether you get a game like Clair Obscur or at launch, you get a disaster like Cyberpunk 2077 and the game's barely playable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately the current market relies <b>a lot</b> on pre-order/release revenue, which I think is a shame, but I agree. And I say that as someone who bought Pokemon Violet at the release and didn't regret, bugs and all, but I had my reasons.<br /> <br /> The game looks ok, but we have a lot to see yet, and the preview and trailer really didn't gave us reason to think it will raise above ok. And it has quite the ground to cover to make it worth the price.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553289#post1553289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, this is what in the biz you would call &quot;not a good look&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>When you can't get Kotaku to talk good about your game, that's kind of a problem.<br /> <br /> And when you can't get them to talk anything at all beyond &quot;day-1 paid DLC sucks&quot;, things really aren't looking promising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T12:42:58-07:00","id":1553298,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Eurogramer posted a video on their YouTube account to, and IME they just read the articles over the video if you want to avoid their cookie policies.<br /> <br /> I still wish there was something more promising about this other than, &quot;Paradox thinks it can at least break even with these marketing tactics,&quot; to glean from all of this. The WoD could use a win, even if it drives people to an edition I don't like, the IP could be doing so much better and it's obvious there's an audience for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T13:07:20-07:00","id":1553299,"title":"","content":"They're paid content makers but I appreciate the Outside Xbox reaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tSCAM6OMWMk?list=FLfWmu27KD5LKzzySKDJidoA\" data-code=\"tSCAM6OMWMk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tSCAM6OMWMk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T13:19:14-07:00","id":1553300,"title":"","content":"It looks alright, it suffers from being bloodlines 2 with all that entails from expectations. It looks like a 6 out if 10 vampire game ignoring its background noise.<br /> <br /> The AAA 90 quid day one dlc leaves a bad taste so I'll wait until the summer steam sale next year. Im having a lot of fun with playing indie horror at 2am so im not in a hurry to cut into my drinking fund for something which looks like dishonoured but wod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-20-2025, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T15:39:01-07:00","id":1553306,"title":"","content":"Yeah, day one DLC is one of the reasons I almost never buy video games on day one anymore, especially when it's something like this - locking a classic clan like the Toreador behind DLC. Instead I almost always wait until we get a sale that bundles everything together six months or a year down the road. I already have plenty of games on my backlog, so there's no need to rush. I'm also not too impressed with what I saw in the preview. The environments look really nice, but the people look pretty wooden and plastic. There is no way this game looks deserving of a $60-$90 price range. I suspect I'll eventually buy this, but probably not for at least a year or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T17:21:43-07:00","id":1553308,"title":"","content":"Im curious what this will entail if the game doesn't perform well. Looking at paradoxes attitude to wod they seem more generally focused on exploiting brand recognition for sales than the products quality or faithfulness to the older stuff (w5 and baali spring to recently mind) but if bloodlines flops or doesn't sell then this strategy is proven as error.<br /> <br /> Although i suspect it will most likely do well enough to continue with that approach for the time being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-20-2025, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T17:44:18-07:00","id":1553310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553300#post1553300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks alright, it suffers from being bloodlines 2 with all that entails from expectations. It looks like a 6 out if 10 vampire game ignoring its background noise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the expectation bias applies so much. I mean, even before all the development problems, it had no chance of living to the name since it was first announced and we knew it wouldn't be made by the same people. As time went on, the &quot;Duke Nuken Forever effect&quot; guaranteed most people I asked really didn't have high expectations.<br /> <br /> At this point, I'd say it exceeds my expectations more than struggles with it.<br /> <br /> My only complain for now is a very personal thing: I <b>HATE</b> First-Person perspective, and &quot;floating hands&quot; only make it worse for me. I didn't like it in the original DOOM, I don't like it here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553306#post1553306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not too impressed with what I saw in the preview. The environments look really nice, but the people look pretty wooden and plastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ain't that true!? In the trailer even more, the graphics are so off for something being released now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T18:44:30-07:00","id":1553313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553308#post1553308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious what this will entail if the game doesn't perform well. Looking at paradoxes attitude to wod they seem more generally focused on exploiting brand recognition for sales than the products quality or faithfulness to the older stuff (w5 and baali spring to recently mind) but if bloodlines flops or doesn't sell then this strategy is proven as error.<br /> <br /> Although i suspect it will most likely do well enough to continue with that approach for the time being.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that we can only speculate on what &quot;perform well&quot; even means for Paradox's bottom line. Someone at Paradox has figured out a number of sales that the game needs to break even, and another for being profitable enough for Paradox to continue to support the game, and another for even considering Paradox continuing WoD games outside of maybe doing a WoD game in their stronger venue of long strategy games. From the outside, we're in the dark about what they're hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T00:37:45-07:00","id":1553319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553308#post1553308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious what this will entail if the game doesn't perform well. Looking at paradoxes attitude to wod they seem more generally focused on exploiting brand recognition for sales than the products quality or faithfulness to the older stuff (w5 and baali spring to recently mind) but if bloodlines flops or doesn't sell then this strategy is proven as error.<br /> <br /> Although i suspect it will most likely do well enough to continue with that approach for the time being.</div> </div> </div> </div>We got a <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/paradox-wants-to-get-out-of-the-rpg-business-if-bloodlines-2-god-willing-is-successful-bloodlines-3-will-be-done-by-someone-else/\" target=\"_blank\">little bit of a preview</a> last year. The tl;dr is that after spending years being a very ambitious publisher that wanted to tackle all sorts of genres, Paradox wants to scale things back and focus on games &quot;they're good at&quot;. Here's an excerpt (The Lilja mentioned here is the deputy CEO of Paradox):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;It is not in our strategic direction to make this kind of game,&quot; Lilja says. &quot;So if Bloodlines 2, God willing, is successful, Bloodlines 3 [will be] done by someone else, on the licence from us. I would say it's the sort of strategic way this would work. So it's still an outlier from what we're supposed to do, we don't know that stuff, so we should probably let other people do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradox has its own small-scale experimental label, Paradox Arc, where it can try different things, but a big RPG doesn't remotely fit that. It would have to be something &quot;very different&quot;, says Lilja, like a CRPG, but even that's a &quot;big investment&quot;, and nowadays expectations are higher than ever thanks to Baldur's Gate 3. So &quot;regardless of outcome,&quot; he says, Bloodlines is a &quot;dead end&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that this will really solve all the problems of Paradox because this doesn't really explain why over the course of the last couple of years Paradox-published games have been failures more often than not. Them being highly ambitious probably was one aspect but there's more to it than that, I'm sure. And so if there's not enough self-reflection on why their publishing-ambitions crashed and burned, I'm not sure a smaller budget alone will fix all the issues. <br /> <br /> Then, of course, you had the resurrection of White Wolf recently and the goal to move everything in-house regarding the WOD (at some point). But we're only at the starting-point of that process, so who knows how this will go... <br /> <br /> I just hope that considering what Paradox was willing to say about Bloodlines 2 last year, they're not gonna end up blaming the Chinese Room if the game &quot;underperforms&quot; or &quot;disappoints&quot; or whatever phrase they want to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T02:48:39-07:00","id":1553321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553319#post1553319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope that considering what Paradox was willing to say about Bloodlines 2 last year, they're not gonna end up blaming the Chinese Room if the game &quot;underperforms&quot; or &quot;disappoints&quot; or whatever phrase they want to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>They licensed the shit out of VTM to questionable results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T08:22:10-07:00","id":1553324,"title":"","content":"Follow up:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/the-chinese-room-defend-bloodlines-2s-paywalled-vampire-clans-we-have-been-expanding-it-from-where-we-originally-planned-to-land-it\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-onl-02.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;fit=crop&amp;enable=upscale&amp;auto=webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/the-chinese-room-defend-bloodlines-2s-paywalled-vampire-clans-we-have-been-expanding-it-from-where-we-originally-planned-to-land-it\" target=\"_blank\"> The Chinese Room defend Bloodlines 2's paywalled vampire clans: \"we have been expanding it from where we originally planned to land it\" </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/the-chinese-room-defend-bloodlines-2s-paywalled-vampire-clans-we-have-been-expanding-it-from-where-we-originally-planned-to-land-it\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/the-chinese-room-defend-bloodlines-2s-paywalled-vampire-clans-we-have-been-expanding-it-from-where-we-originally-planned-to-land-it </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2's current developers attempt to explain why you'll need to pay extra for the Toreador and Lasombra factions. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The answer, broadly, is that the new clans represent additional work on top of The Chinese Room's original plans for the game - sometimes at Paradox's request - so it's fair to flog those bits separately. As for releasing the DLC alongside the main game, which naturally suggests that it could be sold as part of the main game, a PR told James, not in so many words, that they don't want players to have to wait. </div> </div> </div>lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T08:46:15-07:00","id":1553325,"title":"","content":"Oh no... The best response would've been &quot;Guys, you're right, we're sorry. The two Clans will be made available for free.&quot;. The second-best response would've been to simply say nothing. But the worst thing to do in this situation is to go out there and attempt to explain why it makes sense/is actually a good thing. It's like when Ubisoft or EA try to defend their horrible practices. It always ends up with PR-people or CEOs offering out-of-touch corporate-speak justifications that just make the companies look even worse. And then the tone-deaf explanations will generate yet another news-cycle of pointing at the bad/greedy practice.<br /> <br /> The gem from this one is of course &quot;We don't want players to wait.&quot;. That's just silly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T10:07:45-07:00","id":1553326,"title":"","content":"I mean the answer is, &quot;We're charging for this because it was a six year development cycle on THIS version of the game. It's a massive boondoggle we're trying to make our money back on.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is fine as far as I'm concerned.<br /> <br /> It sucks but I'm fully prepared....not to buy the DLC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-21-2025, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T12:28:50-07:00","id":1553336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553325#post1553325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then the tone-deaf explanations will generate yet another news-cycle of pointing at the bad/greedy practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, it's pretty aggravating that they started to throw Paradox under the bus for demanding that TCR add more content which means increased development costs, but then stopped to justify passing the bill on to the customer. <br /> <br /> I don't know what their contract says, so I don't know how much wiggle room TCR had besides shut up and make more stuff, but between the decisions of Paradox and TCR, they added even more work to a product that wasn't part of the desired release initially planned. They made the game more expensive to produce on purpose. They've admitted to it regardless of any spin. <br /> <br /> It's very possible this game comes out and is a good game, but not good enough for these prices. It happens plenty these days. But it's hard to escape bad press when you've admitted you decided to make the game more expensive by adding more content, because unless that content is so good it's worth the price in the eyes of the consumers, there's no value to having spent the money to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T13:18:59-07:00","id":1553343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553336#post1553336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case, it's pretty aggravating that they started to throw Paradox under the bus for demanding that TCR add more content which means increased development costs, but then stopped to justify passing the bill on to the customer.<br /> <br /> I don't know what their contract says, so I don't know how much wiggle room TCR had besides shut up and make more stuff, but between the decisions of Paradox and TCR, they added even more work to a product that wasn't part of the desired release initially planned. They made the game more expensive to produce on purpose. They've admitted to it regardless of any spin.<br /> <br /> It's very possible this game comes out and is a good game, but not good enough for these prices. It happens plenty these days. But it's hard to escape bad press when you've admitted you decided to make the game more expensive by adding more content, because unless that content is so good it's worth the price in the eyes of the consumers, there's no value to having spent the money to make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's revenge for the whole &quot;Bloodlines is a dead end&quot;/&quot;Next time we're gonna work with somebody else.&quot;-talk from last year...? Who knows what's going on... Especially since I also wondered how the contract now looks since the Chinese Room <a href=\"https://www.gamedeveloper.com/business/the-chinese-room-is-independent-again-following-management-buyout\" target=\"_blank\">parted ways with Sumo Digital a couple months ago</a> so now they're fully independent again. But the development-process started when they were still owned by Sumo Digital. Maybe we'll hear more from some developers after the game comes out. <br /> <br /> With the Day 1 DLC, I think it's an unwinnable scenario for Paradox/Chinese Room.<br /> <br /> I see two options:<br /> <br /> Option one: It's not a big deal at all. Once the game comes out, we find out that Clan actually doesn't have that big of an impact on the story. Sure, Phyre will say &quot;I'm from Clan Tremere&quot; or &quot;I'm from Clan Brujah&quot;. You get the occasional remark from other characters but that's about it. The Trainers are there in the hub-world where you can go and buy abilities with XP but outside of that, those characters never turn up in the mainstory, so the absence of the Toreador and Lasombra Trainer NPCs isn't that big of a deal. And when it comes to the costumes, sure you get some extra ones but most of the time you're in first person anyway, so it isn't that big of a deal as well. The only thing you might miss are the abilities.<br /> <br /> But if that's how it is, 30 extra bucks for this seems a bit overpriced.<br /> <br /> Option two: It actually does make a meaningful difference what Clan you're playing. I'm just inventing an example here: There's a scene where a Toreador holds someone hostage and you need to save the hostage. You have some sort of dialogue-tree-puzzle with a countdown-clock where you have to pick the right thing to say to save the hostage. This always plays out the same - except when you've picked Clan Toreador at the beginning. Then you can immediately resolve the situation and it's only in this scenario where you don't end up killing the Toreador to save the hostage. And so you get extra information from that character as well. And the Trainer characters are integrated into the main-story and so the presence of the Lasombra and the Toreador Trainer characters does make a difference and they give you extra insight/context, for example, on what's going on in the story.<br /> <br /> But if that's the case, they're paywalling essential content of the game. It would be like that time when Mass Effect 3 came out and they turned the Prothean companion into separate DLC. I can't imagine playing that game without that character. You get so many cool little story-bits thanks to that character. <br /> <br /> Either way, it was a really bad call in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T13:41:29-07:00","id":1553345,"title":"","content":"There's sorta of a middle ground option (but it's the worst of both) where the impact is highly subjective. We've been told that things like outfits actually do have mechanical impact on the game... but we don't know how much.<br /> <br /> Like, if feeding has a 10% chance of dropping XP (I forgot the V5 term and I don't remember the video game previews even using it when you feed off of the right blood resonance), and the right outfit can bump that up to 15%.<br /> <br /> Can I save scum and reroll feedings as many times as I want? Do combat feedings (which seem very common) count or just hub world feedings? Esp. if it's just hub world feedings... how many of those can I do? How these are played out in practice could make the 5% nothing, something, or a huge deal. And that's going to be subjective to different play styles. People that like to just play the game and see how it goes are going to react differently from people that like to be completionists and explore everything, which will be different from people that like to minmax (esp. if in-game resources can be sparse).<br /> <br /> This is another side of day 1 DLC... the consumers are basically blind on not just the theoretical game-play value of the content, but the personal subjective value it has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T13:43:53-07:00","id":1553346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553319#post1553319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tl;dr is that after spending years being a very ambitious publisher that wanted to tackle all sorts of genres, Paradox wants to scale things back and focus on games &quot;they're good at&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that this will really solve all the problems of Paradox because this doesn't really explain why over the course of the last couple of years Paradox-published games have been failures more often than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a couple things about Paradox:<br /> <br /> 1- They've repeatedly shown that they don't understand a thing about the things they've been trying to do. The very fact that they think (and repeatedly asserted) that a game like <i>Bloodlines</i> has a &quot;short tail&quot; is a statement to how little they understand even the very video-game market beyond their niche. This is their biggest weakness by far, regardless if others can do it, they simply can't. It has been failure after failure as they tackle every possible genre and product in the same way they do their niche, as someone who's both ignorant of things and unwilling to learn. At this point and given their proven inability to learn new tricks, focusing on doing the only things they actually know how to is the only smart decision;<br /> <br /> 2- What do you call a failure? The thing is, while the players' perception is that their games are consistently losing quality over the years, they're actually selling well. Paradox is making good money and keeping up the pace expected by the market. Their shares are at a price as stable as it gets, and they pay their dividends as expected. They seen to have mastered their trade, getting the buck from their investment without either spending too much or failing to do the job;<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, Paradox <b>was</b> over-ambitious and paid the price. It's riddled with problems that it completely failed to address. Their highest dreams lay shattered and, while the problems didn't killed it or even made it poor, they need time to patch things up. They're bad at PR. They're bad at a lot of things. So yeah, they're licking their wounds from all those lost battles and will stay in their safe zone for a while. They are a relatively successful company after all, they became big, so it's not as if keeping their current margins is a bad thing for them. And catering to the previous expectations of gamers simply isn't a winning strategy by now.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this decoupling between consumer expectation/interest and corporate profit isn't even uncommon in the art and entertainment industry.<br /> <br /> Now that's all said and done, all we have to do is wait for the game to actually launch and see what we got. And overall wait for someone else to want to do something, because WoD remains a pet project that only made them loose patience and opportunities for frugal gains, one they don't want to invest so deeply into ever again, as they finally recognize they simply can't make a real profit out from it (even if they still don't recognize it's their own fault).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T15:28:05-07:00","id":1553351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553346#post1553346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2- What do you call a failure? The thing is, while the players' perception is that their games are consistently losing quality over the years, they're actually selling well. Paradox is making good money and keeping up the pace expected by the market. Their shares are at a price as stable as it gets, and they pay their dividends as expected. They seen to have mastered their trade, getting the buck from their investment without either spending too much or failing to do the job;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the games Paradox is publishing. Because I know, their grand-strategy games (who do have some problems of their own, of course) like Stellaris, Crusader Kings, Hearts of Iron etc. are doing quite well. They do have the money to be a somewhat bigger publisher - in theory, at least. Because when you look at what they've been publishing, let's just mention a few: Cities Skyline 2, Prison Architect 2, Lamplighters League, Bloodlines 2, Star Trek: Infinite and the most stark example of them all Life4You. They all have a bit of a &quot;All happy families are alike; each unhappy family is unhappy in its own way.&quot;-type of quality, so each of these games has its own history of failure but then they do have one thing in common: Paradox was the publisher.<ul><li>Cities Skyline 2, disastrous launch, still trying to crawl out of that crater of being a massively disliked follow-up to a classic</li> <li>Prison Architect 2, very troubled development, in the end they switched developers (sound familiar?) and now it's supposed to come out next month</li> <li>Lamplighters League, they had promising developers (Harebrained Schemes who did the Shadowrun games), it was an XCom-style tactical game, buggy at launch, lack of features and then Paradox abandoned it</li> <li>Bloodlines 2... well, that's what this thread is about</li> <li>Star Trek: Infinite, Paradox got the Star Trek license and published a grand strategy game version of Star Trek, ironically it didn't attract a lot of attention because it couldn't compete with the fan-made mods that were made for the Paradox game Stellaris - and so the game got abandoned after a year</li> <li>Life4You, this was supposed to be a Sims-like game, was years (!) in development, Paradox had even created a new studio just for that game - and then last year they announced that the game got cancelled and that very studio was shut down</li> </ul>(If you want a more detailed breakdown, I'd recommend <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CptrqD2jh6c\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a>)<br /> <br /> Or to go further back: Tyranny. That was a CRPG developed by Obsidian (before they were bought by Microsoft) and published by Paradox. Game underperformed and there was supposedly some friction between Paradox and Obsidian. So, keeping in mind what I posted before about Paradox's comments about Bloodlines being a dead end and so on and so forth. Here's an article from 2017 called <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/tyranny/tyranny-sales-paradox-obsidian\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Why didn't Tyranny sell? Paradox on Obsidian's RPG 'everyone was hoping would do better' &quot;</a> and here's an interesting bit from it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even the combination of those factors couldn't translate into mad sales. Speaking at Paradox Con in Stockholm this weekend, the company's top figures voiced disappointment over what they know was a brave and brilliant follow-up to Pillars of Eternity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tyranny did ok,&quot; says Paradox CEO Fred Wester.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're overall ok with it, I think,&quot; echoes Shams Jorjani, Paradox's vice president of business development. &quot;Everyone was hoping that it would do better.&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact, Tyranny's performance at release came in just under the Swedish publisher's expectations.<br /> <br /> &quot;The game's really solid, it still has a lot of interest,&quot; Wester expands. &quot;A lot of people are still on the fence to buy it. I think we will see a long tail on that game with people coming in and playing later on as well. But it didn't really meet the expectations we set for it initially, no.&quot;<br /> <br /> For their part, Obsidian add: &quot;We're very happy that we've made an incredibly deep and unique RPG that players adore, and that while a better reception in the market during a packed holiday season would have been great, we think it's the kind of game that has legs and can do great over time.&quot;<br /> <br /> Next question, then: why didn't Tyranny meet expectations? Wester points to a tough launch window in November - a month in which other great games, including Ubisoft's Watch Dogs 2, struggled to punch through the pre-Christmas noise. Jorjani thinks Tyranny's timing issue goes much broader, arguing that the appetite for '90s style RPGs has already been somewhat sated through crowdfunding.\u200b </div> </div> </div>It's actually kinda funny. Apparently according to Paradox leadership their published games always seem to get released at the wrong time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T16:37:38-07:00","id":1553355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553351#post1553351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the games Paradox is publishing.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Cities Skyline 2</i> sold over 1 million copies. <i>Star Trek: Infinite</i> made a million US dollars in 3 days.<br /> <br /> <i>Life by You</i> and <i>Lamplighters League</i> are precisely what they said: they're outside their comfort zone. Grand Strategy <b>is not</b> the same as a Tactics, so it isn't something they now how to do.<br /> <br /> <i>Prison Architect 2</i> and <i>Bloodlines 2</i> aren't out yet, so we have no means to say anything about them.<br /> <br /> But my point was just that <i>failure</i> isn't a straightforward thing to measure. I'm by no means saying Paradox didn't had some failures, but they're more or less depending on how you define a failure for their games. Or how they do so themselves.<br /> <br /> Either way, my observations were just that, observations.<br /> <br /> Objectively their attempt to do everything everywhere harmed them. They're really, really bad at making games that aren't in their niche, and trying meant dividing attention. So it is possible that the fall in quality came from this lack of focus. However they perceive their faults, their rationale that stepping back will help them correct course makes a lot of sense, even if it isn't necessarily correct.<br /> <br /> And of course, they may still be wrong in many ways and keep &quot;failing&quot;, if still (for now) failing in a way that still makes a lot of money (if below their expectations).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553351#post1553351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's actually kinda funny. Apparently according to Paradox leadership their published games always seem to get released at the wrong time...</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, they have a remarkable ability to not learn anything at all. Although <i>Tyranny</i> specifically may have indeed been the case (as it was overall well received).<br /> <br /> But yeah, they're somehow never personally at fault for under-performance, it's always because something else, and usually a lot of it falls on the game itself, because it's not that they don't know how to make a profit out of other genre, it's the genre that doesn't make profitable games and publishers that work with it make money because they're magical beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T19:06:40-07:00","id":1553360,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> They designed all the clan stuff basically like a DnD game would a class.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Abilities</b><br /> When you choose your clan, you will start with a passive ability unique to each clan. You can then unlock abilities from the Ability Tree, starting with your chosen clan. Each ability requires spending Ability Points to unlock, which are earned from completing missions, combat, and exploration.<br /> At the peak of the Ability Tree, you can unlock the clan Perk, a reward to those dedicated enough to unlock all of the abilities for a clan, giving a permanent passive upgrade. </div> </div> </div>For example Brujah:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Brutality</b><br /> <b>Clan Passive: </b>After feeding, become flushed with vampiric strength, temporarily increasing the power of all your melee attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Taunt</b><br /> Use your supernatural Presence to enrage an opponent or civilian prey, compelling them to attack you. While enraged, the target takes increased damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Charge</b><br /> Surge forward with preternatural speed and rage, grabbing an enemy you collide with to use as a battering ram to knock down others in your path.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Strike</b><br /> Target multiple opponents and unleash an unstoppable hail of punches, with the final strike dealing increased damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Earthshock</b><br /> Slam the ground with explosive force, flinging surrounding enemies into the air.<br /> <br /> <b>Spark of Rage</b><br /> <b>Clan Perk: </b>Killing enemies without feeding still activates your Clan Passive. </div> </div> </div>Will play totally different from Lasombra<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shadow Cloak</b><br /> <b>Clan Passive:</b> Feeding on enemies casts you into shadow, making you harder to see for a period.<br /> <br /> <b>Arms of Ahriman</b><br /> Strike with a thin shadow across the ground. Opponents caught by it will be temporarily trapped in place unless damaged.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Step</b><br /> Step into your own shadow and swiftly emerge from the shadow of your target.<br /> <br /> <b>Glimpse of Oblivion</b><br /> Cause an individual to become afraid, fleeing their post and running from their allies.<br /> <br /> <b>Enter Oblivion</b><br /> Cast a broad shadow ahead of you, then temporarily enter a dimension where only you and others touched by the shadow exist.<br /> <br /> <b>Stygian Shroud</b><br /> <b>Clan Perk:</b> Prevents mortals from attacking you while feeding.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Secondly the Assamite/Banu Haquim video suggests that your Clan will have an effect on the storyline in a direct way, with how the story beats go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zcDEhivcr-w\" data-code=\"zcDEhivcr-w\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zcDEhivcr-w/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-21T21:47:57-07:00","id":1553364,"title":"","content":"*Possible Spoilers* <br /> <br /> Questions about the lore and setting for VTMB2<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> Firstly, let's acknowledge the horrible pricing, day 1 DLC and the changes in how the game feel from both the original VTMB and the unreleased 1st iteration of VTMB2. <br /> <br /> The game looks okish in the previews, but doesn't seem to justify the pricing<br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> Back to the original question:<br /> How is the lore holding up from what is shown in the previews of the game?<br /> <br /> I notice that an NPC mentioned there isn't a Tremere chantry in the city. Which I felt very odd for a camarilla city the size of Seattle. While I did notice on the wiki that Tremeres were only allowed in towards end of 2010s, it still feels very odd.<br /> <br /> It comes across as an excuses to reduce the amount of content needed to flesh out the game, instead of following the lore.<br /> <br /> Can anyone help confirm this?<br /> <br /> And does anyone know of any other lore oddities?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T00:46:20-07:00","id":1553366,"title":"","content":"About the DLC, I got the following mail:<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks to your Blood Points, you\u2019ve earned an upgrade to the Bloodlines 2 Premium Edition! <b>The Bloodlines 2 Base Game must be purchased separately to unlock the additional content.</b><br /> <br /> <b>In order to claim</b> the &quot;Santa Monica Memories Cosmetic Pack&quot; and the &quot;Shadows &amp; Silk Clan Pack&quot; free of charge, please use <b><u>this form</u></b> to choose what platform you want the game keys for, before September 1st.&quot;<br /> <br /> The link doesn't seem to work (yet) btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T02:55:02-07:00","id":1553368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553355#post1553355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Cities Skyline 2</i> sold over 1 million copies. <i>Star Trek: Infinite</i> made a million US dollars in 3 days.<br /> <br /> <i>Life by You</i> and <i>Lamplighters League</i> are precisely what they said: they're outside their comfort zone. Grand Strategy <b>is not</b> the same as a Tactics, so it isn't something they now how to do.<br /> <br /> <i>Prison Architect 2</i> and <i>Bloodlines 2</i> aren't out yet, so we have no means to say anything about them.<br /> <br /> But my point was just that <i>failure</i> isn't a straightforward thing to measure. I'm by no means saying Paradox didn't had some failures, but they're more or less depending on how you define a failure for their games. Or how they do so themselves.<br /> <br /> Either way, my observations were just that, observations.<br /> <br /> Objectively their attempt to do everything everywhere harmed them. They're really, really bad at making games that aren't in their niche, and trying meant dividing attention. So it is possible that the fall in quality came from this lack of focus. However they perceive their faults, their rationale that stepping back will help them correct course makes a lot of sense, even if it isn't necessarily correct.<br /> <br /> And of course, they may still be wrong in many ways and keep &quot;failing&quot;, if still (for now) failing in a way that still makes a lot of money (if below their expectations).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, failure is subjective but importantly, Paradox often calls them failures, then you have the critical reception and fan-response like with Cities Skyline 2 that make that game a failure and sure, you have games that were outside their &quot;comfort zone&quot; but they spent huge on those. That Sims-like game Life4You cost them 200 million dollars in the end and they got nothing out of it. But then you also got cases where Paradox got cold feet way before the release. With Lamplighters League, they bailed on that one before the release and due to that lessening of support 80% of the staff that had worked on it had been let go months before the game even came out. But then it was like a self-fulfilling prophecy with that game because then the developer-team didn't have the appropriate manpower to finish things up and so the game launched with bugs. Or Star Trek Infinite. The critical reception was a bit tepid, the sales were below Paradox's expectations and so after a year they abandoned the game while seemingly having no faith in the project whatsoever.<br /> <br /> That's why I think Paradox is not gonna resolve its issues by staying in their &quot;comfort zone&quot;. Because what in the end makes them failures is that you gotta wonder why it has been so often the case that things don't turn out the way Paradox expects them to? Maybe it would have made more sense to keep supporting Star Trek Infinite and maybe Lamplighter's League could've been salvaged in the last couple of months if the support hadn't been pulled away prematurely. Their strategizing capability is flawed in general, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Or when the leadership in 2017 is like &quot;Jorjani thinks Tyranny's timing issue goes much broader, arguing that the appetite for '90s style RPGs has already been somewhat sated through crowdfunding.&quot; and in 2024 the leadership thinks &quot;Paradox has its own small-scale experimental label, Paradox Arc, where it can try different things, but a big RPG doesn't remotely fit that. It would have to be something &quot;very different&quot;, says Lilja, like a CRPG, but even that's a &quot;big investment&quot;, and nowadays expectations are higher than ever thanks to Baldur's Gate 3. So &quot;regardless of outcome,&quot; he says, Bloodlines is a &quot;dead end&quot;.&quot; Okay, if the leadership is that pessemistic about RPGs - why do they keep holding onto the WOD IP? What does Paradox expect to do with that - except make RPGs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553355#post1553355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said, they have a remarkable ability to not learn anything at all. Although Tyranny specifically may have indeed been the case (as it was overall well received).<br /> <br /> But yeah, they're somehow never personally at fault for under-performance, it's always because something else, and usually a lot of it falls on the game itself, because it's not that they don't know how to make a profit out of other genre, it's the genre that doesn't make profitable games and publishers that work with it make money because they're magical beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's another weird part of Paradox. When something doesn't meet their expectations, they have no problem immediately telling the public and the developers &quot;Nice try - but that didn't work, did it?&quot;. But they act like they're just bystanders and it's all these other things, including the developers, that are responsible for what happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They designed all the clan stuff basically like a DnD game would a class. Secondly the Assamite/Banu Haquim video suggests that your Clan will have an effect on the storyline in a direct way, with how the story beats go. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's one of those things they really should show off in a preview because they just have been saying that that's the case.<br /> <br /> In regards to the abilities... Well, yeah, combat is clearly the focus here. It's not like there's a lockpicking-skill or something like that. And the thing with the abilties as well is that you have these Trainer-characters that also give you access to the other Clans' powers. Depending on what the XP-economy looks like, I guess, you could run into a situation where towards the end you have access to all the powers (except for the Clan-specific passives).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T04:17:04-07:00","id":1553370,"title":"","content":"World Premiere of the first two hours of the game is out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3hP7dCvHpKo\" data-code=\"3hP7dCvHpKo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3hP7dCvHpKo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Without being a shill for the game...it looks fantastic.<br /> <br /> Believe me, my expectations were REALLY LOW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-22T12:25:17-07:00","id":1553380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553360#post1553360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> They designed all the clan stuff basically like a DnD game would a class.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd describe that more as &quot;designed like an action video-game&quot; than as D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> That's a departure from the original Bloodlines, as that game really tried to be as true to the tabletop system as possible, but I don't think a comparison to another tabletop really works here.<br /> <br /> By itself it isn't bad, if it does make for a better video-game experience, but that we shall see.<br /> <br /> And the ability teachers, I'm on the fence on that. On one hand, spelled out like that it sounds quite contrived, but it may have a better execution than this shallow description. On the other hand, it does play on the idea that Kindred can learn OoC Disciplines, but need help to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553364#post1553364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the lore holding up from what is shown in the previews of the game?<br /> <br /> I notice that an NPC mentioned there isn't a Tremere chantry in the city. Which I felt very odd for a camarilla city the size of Seattle. While I did notice on the wiki that Tremeres were only allowed in towards end of 2010s, it still feels very odd.<br /> <br /> It comes across as an excuses to reduce the amount of content needed to flesh out the game, instead of following the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think those are fair concerns, to be honest, at least not in the way you put it.<br /> <br /> First, the setting's lore is dynamic and varied. Cities without a Chantry may exist for a variety of reasons, as may any other peculiarities in the game's lore. The original Bloodlines itself was full of oddities, including the very presence of LaCroix (as weak as he was politically) in one of the main Anarch Free States.<br /> <br /> Second, stories are multi-purpose things. There's nothing wrong in making stuff to justify content, mechanics, or their lack thereof. This is normal. Deviating from standard lore is also normal.<br /> <br /> There's merit in wondering if the game will have a good story or not. I don't think we currently have enough data to guess one way or another. It's also valid to complain about the lack of a Chantry if you really wanted one (I do think it would have been cool). But &quot;lore oddities&quot; aren't a bad thing by themselves.<br /> <br /> And as far as I know, there aren't many info on the game's lore, yet. There's a Malk in Phyre's head, which is weird, and by the Banu Haqim trailer it seems her backstory changes with clan, which is cool.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553368#post1553368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox often calls them failures</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said before that their dreams lie shattered.<br /> <br /> One pattern that I see in their blunders over the years is that Paradox dreamed high. Like, really high, as in completely unreal expectations.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they though their niche is the most challenging there is and so their success meant they could do anything, or what, but the thing isn't just that they aren't doing things well, but that they were consistently setting their ambitions far above anything reasonable.<br /> <br /> Paradox did this in two main ways. First, they tried to do everything without knowing shit about that particular market, with delusional confidence that their standard methods would do just fine, the outcome would be outstanding, and they freely put money without &quot;testing the waters&quot; first with minor projects.<br /> <br /> Second, that anything short of astounding success was seen as failure followed by frustrated tantrums. And that plays on what I said because much of their perceived failures aren't nearly that bad. <i>Skylines 2</i> and <i>Infinite </i>are perfectly serviceable games. <i>Tyranny</i> was a solid entry in the RPG market that could develop into a franchise (being already a continuation). In fact, as far as we can see right now, even <i>Bloodlines 2</i> has an actual chance of being good, or at least would were it not for their launch strategy to be already geared towards recouping loss and never looking back at it again. Any time things don't go exactly as planned they deem it a failure, at the same time that those plans are excessively ambitious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553368#post1553368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their strategizing capability is flawed in general</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. At this point, I think this isn't just an opinion anymore, it's an objective fact.<br /> <br /> They don't know when to start, when to quit, how much dedicate to something, or how to analyze what caused their problems.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553368#post1553368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, if the leadership is that pessemistic about RPGs - why do they keep holding onto the WOD IP? What does Paradox expect to do with that - except make RPGs?</div> </div> </div> </div>To cut them some slack, it doesn't have to be RPGs just because the IP was born for TTRPGs. The fact that they don't have a single actual project as they wait and wait for third parties to come wanting to license the IP for something big that never comes is a problem on itself, but has nothing to do with them not wanting to do RPGs specifically.<br /> <br /> But more to the point... it's a pet project. It has never been anything but a pet project. They bought the IP because their CEO wanted it, and they keep it more or less for the same reason. At this point the most that can be said as far as market strategy goes is that they don't want to sell it lower than they bought, and so they'll keep making small change through TT books and licensing low-budget indie games as long as it lets them make slightly more money from the IP than it costs in taxes.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553370#post1553370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without being a shill for the game...it looks fantastic.<br /> <br /> Believe me, my expectations were REALLY LOW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say fantastic, but it's definitely above any previous expectations. At the very least it has a good chance of being at least half decent. And it may even be really good, although it'll hardly be worth the full price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T02:00:22-07:00","id":1553394,"title":"","content":"It looks like what I suspected 6 maybe 7 out of 10 generic vampire game. Something I'll grab on steam summer sale next year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T06:02:47-07:00","id":1553397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553394#post1553394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like what I suspected 6 maybe 7 out of 10 generic vampire game. Something I'll grab on steam summer sale next year.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go so far as an 8 because it's got the atmosphere of V:TM down and strong characters so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T13:53:20-07:00","id":1553406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553397#post1553397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd go so far as an 8 because it's got the atmosphere of V:TM down and strong characters so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's still too soon to call an 8.<br /> <br /> Not saying it isn't possible, what we have now does have a good enough chance of getting there, but talking bets I would stay on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Ragged Robin</a>'s more conservative side. 6, maybe 7. There's a chance of something better, but there's a chance of something worse, too.<br /> <br /> And we'll see with time if the DLC is any good. That'll depend on two factors being true at the same time:<br /> <br /> 1- The game must be complete. Playing with the four available clans has to give enough lore and closure. If the two extra clans gatekeep a portion of the lore of the game, to the point of you feeling that you didn't complete it without those pieces, then that's BS and the game itself isn't worth it;<br /> <br /> 2- Clans must make a pretty significant difference in the play through. If two clans cost half-again the price of the game, they must add a lot of effective content.<br /> <br /> Personally I think this is a tall order, although not something unfeasible. Everything we have by now indicates this may very well be the case. Lets see how it plays out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T14:15:08-07:00","id":1553407,"title":"","content":"Sadly, there's going to be no DLC according to Paradox.<br /> <br /> It's like spider-man 2 in that they planned to but the behind the scenes disasters seem to have meant they already are writing this off. <br /> <br /> Which is a shame because I'm loving what I've seen so far of the plot and social interactions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T14:23:25-07:00","id":1553408,"title":"","content":"The dialogue is corny trash; has that formulaic triple AAA graphical aesthetic look to it; choppy animations that somehow come off as less organic than its predecessor game; a named protagonist instead of an unnamed one, in which the player could have immersed themselves into (said named pre-determined character also has no real presence or anything that would garner player interest into them, aside from being an Elder.. who also admittedly seems written not as an actual Elder, but a phoned-in); and on top of all that (with many other gripes I have, that I will not exhaustively list, as the shown previous list was already getting too long) it is asking for <i><b>DAY 1 DLC</b></i> for a shaky game that even Paradox suspects will not sell well. <br /> <br /> The most belligerent of it all from said Day 1 DLC, is the fact that they are locking the <i><b>Toreador</b></i>, one of the classic VTM Clans, behind that paywall. The malignance of Day 1 DLC has increasingly become a fact in the gaming industry (at least the mainstream AAA sphere of it), something I despise but have to accept as a reality; locking the Lasombra in this Day 1 DLC scheme would make sense at least, since they are a unique clan that used to be Sabbat (a V5 idiocratic development, but that is a rant for another time and one I have done already in the past) and they have unique powers that are definitely &quot;DLC-coded&quot; from how apart in power and utility their signature discipline (Obtenebration) match against the more classic Clans...<br /> <br /> ...but the Toreador? The Toreador? <br /> <br /> Nothing about this game will be good. Nothing about it &quot;captures the atmosphere of V:tM&quot;. That atmosphere has not been a thing since the release of V5. This game is an exemplar of that killed atmosphere continued. It's just a corny, trash cash grab with the Bloodlines label on the box, which has been a common x5 edition tactic of Parawolf adapted to the video game format as can be plainly seen here. An 80-year-old man at a nursing home who has only been brushed up with near basics of the Storyteller system could ST a game with better &quot;V:tM atmosphere&quot; than what they are doing here.<br /> <br /> No ability to play as the Gangrel. No ability to play as Malkavian (both of which will probably be rendered as future DLC, if this game even broaches far from being a complete financial disaster). No real character customization. Just generally a milquetoast pre-determined protagonist that, like I've mentioned above before, does not seem interesting. At all. A pre-determined protagonist at least has to have something that draws the player into finding them cool or palpable to play as if there is an exclusion to making your own character. <br /> <br /> Who is this game actually for? What is Paradox, and by extension The Chinese Room after taking up the mantle to finish this game, trying to reach out to? Another &quot;mainstream&quot; audience like they tried to achieve with V5? How can that be achieved, when an outsider looking outside at Bloodlines 2, finds nothing about it appealing at all? All Paradox has is shills-upon-shills and backchannels to many of the &quot;game media&quot; journalist companies, but that can go only so far; especially with the negative reception from the Day 1 DLC nonsense. <br /> <br /> This game is going to be a disaster.<br /> <br /> At least I'll gain some entertainment from the +1 hourlong critic YouTube reviews that will be absolutely scorching it on release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T15:08:59-07:00","id":1553412,"title":"","content":"Getting confirmation that the name &quot;Phyre&quot; is just something the character stole from a poster right after waking up blunts the silliness of the name a bit in my mind; as does dialogue that indicates that the character has a few sobriquets they're more commonly known by among the kindred. I think it's not a bad decision if you want a voiced protagonist for them to be using an established alias to hide their true identity and most vampires only know names like &quot;the Nomad&quot; as the real deal. It does a decent balancing act of &quot;player can insert themselves&quot; and &quot;we can write dialogue that doesn't have to constantly dance around a nameless protagonist.&quot;<br /> <br /> All of the previews so far are explicitly from a pre-release build for early reviewers to get a taste. So there's some expected jank to the animations that should be (not will be, but should be, and we'll see if) fixed at true launch.<br /> <br /> We're definitely in a wait and see mode, but there is clearly going to be issues with (a) actually impressing an audience that has seen this game at this quality a few dozen times already and (b) starting off on the bad foot of various PR issues we've already brought up. The game is stuck in a very bad position where it needs to be a fantastic game to avoid getting thrashed... or worse just forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T15:39:12-07:00","id":1553413,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's funny with all the complaints about having a named protagonist given the protagonist...doesn't have a name.<br /> <br /> Just an alias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T17:21:29-07:00","id":1553417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553413#post1553413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's funny with all the complaints about having a named protagonist given the protagonist...doesn't have a name.<br /> <br /> Just an alias.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing funny, as only now we know for sure it's an alias. While I weren't really pissed off about that, I can't say the complaints were aimless at their time.<br /> <br /> But overall there's very little chance that the game will be a success, and not because it seems it will be bad (given previous expectations, it seems even promising). The whole story behind it plus the bad decisions on pricing, DLC, and preemptively declaring they won't work on it any further, the game has an almost impossible battle ahead to be a success.<br /> <br /> And Paradox won't learn a thing with it, or realize the &quot;failure&quot; is due to their own decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T01:29:16-07:00","id":1553420,"title":"","content":"I've watched that two hour gameplay video... For me, I'd give that experience a 6 out of 10. Hopefully, the animations, both in combat and outside of it, will look better at launch. Other than that... it isn't bad but it's not great either. There's nothing that really stood out for me in those two hours.<br /> <br /> One thing that concerned me was feeding in combat. Because when you feed, you go into third-person and this animation plays - but during that animation you can still take damage (I think it's around the 1 hour 1 minute mark where you see that). And I also noticed when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26219\" data-vbnamecard=\"26219\">Aydoo</a> mentioned the Lasombra powers they have this Passive &quot;Stygian Shroud Clan Perk: Prevents mortals from attacking you while feeding.&quot;. I'd hoped that damage during feeding would knock you out of the animation at least. But it seems like once you give the prompt, you're stuck in the animation and enemies can still attack you. Like, you're in the feeding-animation and you see your healthbar shrink. Especially with bigger damage-dealers around. That could be potentially annoying. <br /> <br /> I think the biggest issue I had with the two hours is that Phyre in those two hours has the charisma of a wet blanket. Hopefully, by you making choices and getting more fully involved with the story, this will get better. But during those first two hours, if I had to pick, I'd have preferred to just straight up play as Fabien. At least, you got a genuine character there. <br /> <br /> Phyre being an alias is more believable - but I still don't like it. It's just that everyone has realistic names so this fantasy-ish name always sticks out like a sore thumb. At that point, I'd much rather would've preferred for Phyre to call themselves the &quot;Nomad&quot; or vague stuff like that, if we go with the alias-idea (either because she doesn't remember her name or the character's real name will be relevant later on or something like that). <br /> <br /> Also, I remember from a dev-blog that they talked about items to use during combat but I absolutely did not expect this game to have a potion-system. Always assumed it would be something more realistic like blood-bags, for example. I mean it's a convenient shortcut as far as game-mechanics are concerned but man, potions... this is a game with potions. Definitely did not see that coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T02:02:15-07:00","id":1553422,"title":"","content":"Wait. If the alias, Phyre, was taken from a poster... Does this means we could have had a protagonist called Taylor Swift, if it had been a Taylor Swift poster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T09:17:42-07:00","id":1553425,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what the title says, I've watched a couple of the playthroughs and have made a summary of the events as well as list for what the differences are. You can judge what is important and what is not from what I've seen.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> * Phyre wakes up in torpor in Seattle but wasnt in America when they were transported. They kill the person who awakens them and another security watchmen. The tutorial consists of also evading the cops after your initial murder.<br /> <br /> * They discover they have Fabian the Malkavian Noir Detective in their head.<br /> <br /> * Phyre is a pseudonym they pick from a Seattle grunge band poster and they are the Nomad.<br /> <br /> * You've been in torpor since the 1920. Fabien was embraced around then and has never left Seattle. This will become important because Fabien and you will be doing different parts of the game. Phyre will be doing the politics and beating while Fabien will be doing the flashbacks and investigation.<br /> <br /> * There's actually no mystery for Fabian or it's solved quickly, Fabian was the one who awoke Phyre and they diablerized him. You find Fabien's corpse soon after, which is lore breaking because it should have disintegrated at Fabien's age.<br /> <br /> * Phyre is aware that Fabian still existing in their consciousness is weird and describes how diablerie normally works. There's a symbol on Phyre's hand that doesn't seem to be overtly magical at this point.<br /> <br /> * Phre has an encounter with the Sheriff, Benny Muldoon, who is a psychopath who is on a crusade to kill every Thin Blood in Seattle. He hates manners and is a Brujah I assume. Phyre can stand up to him or try to be polite.<br /> <br /> * Phyre goes to present themselves to the Prince but Fabian warns against that. Instead, they decide to visit the ex-Prince, Lou Graham, instead. Lou abdicated being prince, which Pyre and Fabian both find unusual. However, the new prince is her childe so it shouldn't be too surprising to seasoned VTM players.<br /> <br /> * There's a massive snowstorm that has isolated Seattle for the events of the game.<br /> <br /> * Phyre heads to Lou Graham's hotel and has a flashback to the 1920s when she was Prince and Fabrian was newly Embraced. This is a hint that, in fact, you are going to be playing Fabien as much as Phyre.<br /> <br /> * Phyre meets Lou who has just slaughtered a bunch of Anarchs who attacked her haven.<br /> <br /> * Lou will comment if you're not changed to nicer clothes after waking up from 100 years of torpor.<br /> <br /> * The Prince of Seattle, JJ Campbell, has been murdered by the &quot;Anarchs.&quot; Lou isn't too worried because she's installed her other childe as Prince. You piss off Lou if you question her in anything but a flattering way. She's described as a narcissistic psychopath--so a typical Elder.<br /> <br /> * The new prince is Ryong Choi.<br /> <br /> * The game is reactive to your Clan and if you're polite and differential to Lou but a Brujah, Fabien will comment on it.<br /> <br /> * You head to the Prince's skyscraper and find out it's under assault by the Anarchs too. Phyre proceeds to lay the smack down on them. So I don't think you'll be very friendly with the Anarchs. Fabien comments on how the Anarchs aren't normally dangerous and them agreeing each other other, let alone coordinating to kill the Prince is insane.<br /> <br /> * Along the way you meet Tolly killing a bunch of Anarchs and their ghouls. The Nosferatu talks like a flamboyant stereotype, which is an odd juxtaposition. He's not the Sheriff but one of the Deputies like Fabien was.<br /> <br /> * You meet Safia the Tremere in a computer server room as you climb your way up an elevator shaft. She's a super Nomad fanboy and you have the option to flirt with her or scare the shit out of her.<br /> <br /> * You meet Ryong interrogating an Anarch Thin Blood who knows nothing that Ryong kills. Ryong is a weak prince and needs to punish you for the tutorial but doesn't have a sheriff. You aren't made sheriff immediately but it's pretty obvious she's alreadying thining its a compromise. Ryong is just Lou Graham's puppet anyway and mentioning her makes it clear Ryong feels manipulated.<br /> <br /> * You head back to Fabien's apartment and finds its a hellhole that is covered in police tape. You go to sleep...and find yourself in a vision of a sunny garden where someone is talking to you.<br /> <br /> * You flashback to Fabien's past in 2024 as a police detective vampire working to keep the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> * You learn how to wipe minds in-game. You use it to wipe the memory of a police detective you owe $30, which shows Fabien is a dick.<br /> <br /> * Fabien then investigates a masquerade breach with a pretty young ghoul who may be using Elif's model. Sadly, she's killed by the Second Inquisition before the end of the flashback. The mystery is determining who sent her to the club since it was to pass on a message to you. You can speak with her ghost. She's a dumb valley girl but I feel like it's a waste because I wanted to keep her as my own ghoul.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T09:18:20-07:00","id":1553426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553422#post1553422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. If the alias, Phyre, was taken from a poster... Does this means we could have had a protagonist called Taylor Swift, if it had been a Taylor Swift poster?</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire named Taylor, yes. Fabien probably would have commented on the Swift part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T09:21:58-07:00","id":1553427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553420#post1553420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've watched that two hour gameplay video... For me, I'd give that experience a 6 out of 10. Hopefully, the animations, both in combat and outside of it, will look better at launch. Other than that... it isn't bad but it's not great either. There's nothing that really stood out for me in those two hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Six out of ten seems massively unfair but your opinion is your opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing that concerned me was feeding in combat. Because when you feed, you go into third-person and this animation plays - but during that animation you can still take damage (I think it's around the 1 hour 1 minute mark where you see that). And I also noticed when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26219\" data-vbnamecard=\"26219\">Aydoo</a> mentioned the Lasombra powers they have this Passive &quot;Stygian Shroud Clan Perk: Prevents mortals from attacking you while feeding.&quot;. I'd hoped that damage during feeding would knock you out of the animation at least. But it seems like once you give the prompt, you're stuck in the animation and enemies can still attack you. Like, you're in the feeding-animation and you see your healthbar shrink. Especially with bigger damage-dealers around. That could be potentially annoying. </div> </div> </div>It's definitely the game incentivizing that you don't feed in the middle of combat but should during stealth or while not surrounded by enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the biggest issue I had with the two hours is that Phyre in those two hours has the charisma of a wet blanket. Hopefully, by you making choices and getting more fully involved with the story, this will get better. But during those first two hours, if I had to pick, I'd have preferred to just straight up play as Fabien. At least, you got a genuine character there. </div> </div> </div>I note that Phyre being a pretty stereotypical Dracula type of vampire was actually pretty cool. I especially like their accent is kind of three different kinds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Phyre being an alias is more believable - but I still don't like it. It's just that everyone has realistic names so this fantasy-ish name always sticks out like a sore thumb. At that point, I'd much rather would've preferred for Phyre to call themselves the &quot;Nomad&quot; or vague stuff like that, if we go with the alias-idea (either because she doesn't remember her name or the character's real name will be relevant later on or something like that). </div> </div> </div>The choices include the option of trying to hide that you're the Nomad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I remember from a dev-blog that they talked about items to use during combat but I absolutely did not expect this game to have a potion-system. Always assumed it would be something more realistic like blood-bags, for example. I mean it's a convenient shortcut as far as game-mechanics are concerned but man, potions... this is a game with potions. Definitely did not see that coming. </div> </div> </div>The potions are canon in 5th Edition and made by the local Thin Bloods and the blood trade. It's also a game that heavily focuses on Resonance. Which means that it's Paradox who said it needed to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T10:16:37-07:00","id":1553430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553427#post1553427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely the game incentivizing that you don't feed in the middle of combat but should during stealth or while not surrounded by enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually, you're gonna have to feed quite a lot during combat. Go to that video at 1 hour 1 minute that you posted before. You see those abilities at the bottom right that you call up with left trigger. They have these little notches beneath them. One has two, the other three. You use an ability and the notches are empty. The way it works is that every time you feed, you fill one of those notches and when they're filled, you can use the ability again.<br /> <br /> So you are supposed to feed during combat. And quite a lot in fact. Hence my concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553427#post1553427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that Phyre being a pretty stereotypical Dracula type of vampire was actually pretty cool. I especially like their accent is kind of three different kinds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, my impression was more of her characterization feeling like flavorless slob. But that's the impression I got from those first two hours. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553427#post1553427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The choices include the option of trying to hide that you're the Nomad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh come on, I'm sure we both have played our share of RPGs over the last couple of years. Stuff like that is no guarantee for any sort of depth. I remember when I played Dragon Age Veilguard last year, for example, you got the &quot;Elf&quot;-dialogue-option when your character's an Elf or the Mage-dialogue-option when your class is Mage. Stuff like that. But it's there for flavor. Nothing else. <br /> <br /> We will find out when we play the game how deep it truly is. But really, like I said, I'm sure we both have played our share of RPGs. You must know how illusory the veneer of depth can be with these things. Just because the game gives you three different options of what to say doesn't necessarily mean that there's any choice happening at all. Your character says something different based on your choice and the response is different. Except it always leads to the same outcome - no matter which one of the three options you've picked. That happens so often with these systems. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553427#post1553427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potions are canon in 5th Edition and made by the local Thin Bloods and the blood trade. It's also a game that heavily focuses on Resonance. Which means that it's Paradox who said it needed to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've been thinking. At one point, Fabien was supposed to be a Thinblood. Maybe it's a remnant of that. In that version, Fabien (as a Thinblood) would help you with his knowledge of Thinblooded Alchemy and that's how you'd get the Potion system. <br /> <br /> But even so, it's a very stereotypical potion system. Healing-potion, damage-boost potion... I wish the presentation would've been a bit more flavorful (like the stuff from Blood Sigils). But as a mechanic... why not? More options during combat are always good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T15:08:06-07:00","id":1553432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553397#post1553397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd go so far as an 8 because it's got the atmosphere of V:TM down and strong characters so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's what got it up to maybe 7, if 5th ed taught me one thing is that atmosphere will only take you so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T06:30:32-07:00","id":1553480,"title":"","content":"Yesterday I read the news that the reception to Lasombra and Toreador being locked behind a day 1 DLC is so bad that Paradox is \u2018\u2019Listening to Feedback\u2019\u2019 and that they are \u2018\u2019making adjustment ahead of launch.\u2019\u2019<br /> <br /> Might be nothing might be something. I'll keep being cautiously optimistic.<br /> <br /> On another note.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m so starved for a good VTM action game that I\u2019ll probably end up buying it. I\u2019ll just wait and see how the state of the game is and how much I think it\u2019s worth. I don\u2019t play the game as much as I used to do, so I can definitely wait until a sale.<br /> <br /> From what I\u2019ve heard from people, it seems like the current issue with the game is that it\u2019s called Bloodline 2 and it has little to do with Bloodline. If it was its own thing, it probably wouldn\u2019t get that much flak.<br /> <br /> I had the same sentiment for Baldur\u2019s gate 3. The game was definitely amazing, probably even more so than the original game(hard to compare), but it simply wasn\u2019t \u2018\u2019Baldur\u2019s Gate 3\u2019\u2019. It could have been named Baldur\u2019s Gate : Rise of the Absolute and I would have been fine with it, but naming it Baldur\u2019s Gate 3, felt like they tried to present the game like a sequel, when it clearly was not. It\u2019s a spiritual successor, at best. Again, still an amazing game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T07:03:40-07:00","id":1553481,"title":"","content":"Regarding the name &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;, I thought <a href=\"https://gameinformer.com/exclusive-interview/2025/08/15/what-makes-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-a-bloodlines-game\" target=\"_blank\">this interview on Gameinformer</a> with Creative Director Alex Skidrow was interesting:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I ask creative director Alex Skidmore why the game is called Bloodlines 2 instead of something else, he thinks for a while, then starts his answer by saying, &quot;It's what we were asked to do.&quot; It's an honest response. Notoriously, Bloodlines 2 was originally being made by Hardsuit Labs and got far enough in development to be shown at E3 2019, but the next two years were filled with delays, departures, and ultimately, the decision to remove Hardsuit Labs from the project entirely. The Chinese Room took its place, and since it was working on a project that had already been announced, it didn't have much of a choice \u2013 this game would always be called Bloodlines 2. </div> </div> </div>So, according to this, the series of events appears to be: The Chinese Room wanted to make a VtM-game. They got approval from Paradox. They started to work on it. Then Paradox approached them and told them the game they're working on would now be called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;. I wonder how much the trajectory of development was impacted by Paradox deciding that the Chinese Room project would be called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;... <br /> <br /> Also, it will be interesting to see how far they're willing to go in addressing the fan-feedback regarding the paywalled essential content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T13:29:34-07:00","id":1553491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553480#post1553480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be nothing might be something. I'll keep being cautiously optimistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's fair. I wouldn't bet on it, but there's nothing to lose hoping for the best.<br /> <br /> The worse they can do is throw in the DLC some &quot;extra content&quot; so stupid as to infuriate people all over again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553480#post1553480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m so starved for a good VTM action game that I\u2019ll probably end up buying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it seems promising enough that, even if it isn't worth the full price, I think a lot of people here will just wait for a sale.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> may disagree with ratings like 6 out of 10, but that's still a game worth playing, and worth buying at <i>some</i> price.<br /> <br /> Do I think it'll be a disaster launch? Yes. But it has more to do now with marketing strategy than actual game quality. Game quality, it seems good enough for now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553480#post1553480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it seems like the current issue with the game is that it\u2019s called Bloodline 2 and it has little to do with Bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a fair complaint at this point, with neither of the two games.<br /> <br /> While having a connection to the first story would have been really nice, both <i>Bloodlines</i> are connected by overall game play, modern setting and focus on city politics (in some way). Other than that... we all know the story of its development. We all know it is called <i>Bloodlines</i> because it was meant to be called <i>Bloodlines</i> from the beginning, and it's a matter of honor more than anything. And that The Chinese Room took a project mid-development to work with without fundamentally changing what the project is about.<br /> <br /> At this point this is a Ship of Theseus <i>Bloodlines</i>. Any resemblance to the original game is a miracle beyond expectation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553480#post1553480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the same sentiment for Baldur\u2019s gate 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most D&amp;D video game franchises are defined by the immediate setting to begin with. On top of that, they're official to the continuing setting and must follow it, but are not the only things advancing said setting. BG3 happens around the city of Baldur's Gate. It has characters from the area, including some from previous games. It revisits items and areas. And it is again running around the Bhaalspawn and Bhaal's machinations. And it follows the TTRPG rules. Why can't it be called the 3rd installment of the franchise?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it couldn't or shouldn't have more links to the previous games, nor am I saying it couldn't be named with a subtitle. But I find it hard to justify that it shouldn't be called &quot;3&quot; because it isn't sufficiently a continuation.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553481#post1553481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much the trajectory of development was impacted by Paradox deciding that the Chinese Room project would be called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense, everything.<br /> <br /> Whatever their pitch was, from day 1 it was only accepted as a continuation of the <i>Bloodlines 2</i> project.<br /> <br /> The whole thing was predicated on it being called that, it's impossible to say how much it impacted because it's impossible to disentangle the two things.<br /> <br /> As much as there may have been moments when they wanted to call the game something else, I really doubt this was ever on the table for real, this statement seems more like damage reduction from their own PR (&quot;blaming&quot; Paradox on as many problems as possible) than anything with actual relevance. The very question is kinda dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T18:09:31-07:00","id":1553498,"title":"","content":"Paradox may be revisiting the cash gate thing as well (which was imposed on the Chinese Room anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T18:12:10-07:00","id":1553499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553491#post1553491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> may disagree with ratings like 6 out of 10, but that's still a game worth playing, and worth buying at <i>some</i> price.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I'm a very forgiving reviewer, but I tend to view 6 out of 10 as, &quot;BARELY worth playing at any price&quot; <br /> <br /> 8 out of 10 is more, &quot;I liked it&quot;<br /> <br /> While 9 out of 10 and 10 out of 10 is &quot;I loved it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other people believe the latter must be perfect games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T19:38:08-07:00","id":1553501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553491#post1553491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">may disagree with ratings like 6 out of 10, but that's still a game worth playing, and worth buying at <i>some</i> price.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I hate the most about videogame-critique/journalism is how outlets like IGN or Gamespot popularized the idea that anything less than an 8 out of 10 is an expression of &quot;I hate this game&quot;. And you see that in the industry as well. Because there are companies out there that tie paying a bonus to developers based on Metacritic scores. The most infamous example is, of course, Fallout: New Vegas. There, the bonus was tied to a Metacritic score of 85 - but the game got an 84. <br /> <br /> I always thought this feels a bit narrow-minded. At that point, why even bother with a 10-point score? And then I can understand the people who feel that not using scores at all is the better option. Especially when they're used like this. <br /> <br /> To me, 5 out of 10 means average. There's good stuff, there's bad stuff - but overall it's just a &quot;take it or leave it&quot; shrug. 6 to 7 is &quot;I like it - but there are big problems here that we need to talk about&quot;. 8 means &quot;I love this game&quot;. And 9 to 10 is &quot;Not only do I love this but this is &quot;Best of the Year&quot;-material&quot; with a 10 maybe being even more than that. Anything below 5 is where you get to &quot;I hate this&quot;. 4 means &quot;The bad clearly outweighs the good here&quot;. And with 3 or less, it's games where something's fundamentally wrong, stuff like sections that are literally unplayable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553491#post1553491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a sense, everything.<br /> <br /> Whatever their pitch was, from day 1 it was only accepted as a continuation of the <i>Bloodlines 2</i> project.<br /> <br /> The whole thing was predicated on it being called that, it's impossible to say how much it impacted because it's impossible to disentangle the two things.<br /> <br /> As much as there may have been moments when they wanted to call the game something else, I really doubt this was ever on the table for real, this statement seems more like damage reduction from their own PR (&quot;blaming&quot; Paradox on as many problems as possible) than anything with actual relevance. The very question is kinda dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be interesting to read a post-mortem about what happened here exactly. The thing that still baffles me is the Paradox-con last year when you got these comments like &quot;Bloodlines is a dead end&quot; and &quot;If we're gonna make a Bloodlines 3, we gotta work with somebody else.&quot;. Who knows how much acrimony there is between Paradox and the Chinese Room at this point? And I'm just thinking back to their relationship with Obsidian and how that turned sour. Paradox really has a gift in pushing developers away after they've worked with them. And it's all simply because these developers didn't fulfill their unrealistic expectations. Not unrealistic in the sense that it was technically impossible but unrealistic in the sense that Paradox isn't capable of steering/managing projects that capably. <br /> <br /> Especially when you consider that when Paradox bought the WOD IP it didn't come with a clause saying &quot;You HAVE to make a big budget RPG called Bloodlines 2.&quot; and when things with Hardsuit Labs fell apart, there was no legal contract lying around saying &quot;You HAVE to release a game called Bloodlines 2.&quot;. To only start handwringing about the whole thing last year and getting cold feet now just feels so bad. It's the definition of &quot;too little, too late&quot;. They should've considered this years ago but instead, getting this game finally on the market has just turned into yet another misstep in the whole saga with this paywalled core content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T20:56:16-07:00","id":1553505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553498#post1553498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox may be revisiting the cash gate thing as well (which was imposed on the Chinese Room anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's hope it. I don't think they will, but lets hope so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553499#post1553499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, I'm a very forgiving reviewer, but I tend to view 6 out of 10 as, &quot;BARELY worth playing at any price&quot;<br /> <br /> 8 out of 10 is more, &quot;I liked it&quot;<br /> <br /> While 9 out of 10 and 10 out of 10 is &quot;I loved it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other people believe the latter must be perfect games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there isn't an objective measure for us to say what's correct.<br /> <br /> For whatever it's worth, I'm unforgiving with the numbers because I think the full range must be meaningful, and there must be room to distinguish between levels of good.<br /> <br /> So a 5 for me already means &quot;achieved the basic goal&quot;. If the goal is to be entertaining, well, it was. In this case, that's enough to say it's worth some money, even if not necessarily what's being asked.<br /> <br /> Above 5 then means I find it good, even if not great. I'll play it, and I wouldn't mind playing it again someday. Even, as a completionist, if &quot;plating&quot; it isn't too tiresome I'll probably do it.<br /> <br /> 8 is already <b>really</b> good for me, sometimes even a candidate for Game of the Year if the year in question hasn't been great. If I give 8 to a game, I think it's not just worth the price, but worth going out of your way to get it.<br /> <br /> 9 and 10 are too special for me. Those are the best of the best. I do think 10 is perfection, because I'm against the idea of &quot;creating&quot; ratings above the top of the scale, for me that goes against the purpose of the scale to begin with, so how do I say a game is above and beyond the competition? If I gave 10 to something, I don't believe you can meaningfully compare them to other games, any aspect you dislike of it is probably because you dislike the very premises behind that aspect.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553501#post1553501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things I hate the most about videogame-critique/journalism is how outlets like IGN or Gamespot popularized the idea that anything less than an 8 out of 10 is an expression of &quot;I hate this game&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has a history that goes way back, before even the internet was a thing, or video-games.<br /> <br /> While I also dislike it, it's unfair to put the blame solely on the industry, they're just reacting to how people got used to read those scales.<br /> <br /> People don't like to give bad reviews if they're not really pissed. This changes a little with culture, but never seems to really vanish as a trend, people simply don't feel it's right. That's why in 5-stars reviews, 3 stars are rare, 2 stars are almost unheard of.<br /> <br /> So usually the rationale of most people is to give max or near max ratings, then subtract as they think of aspects they really disliked. Only if pissed they'll do the opposite, either start from half or minimum and make their way from there.<br /> <br /> Most simply have no objective or almost-objective criteria for rating. Then outlets have to work with it, giving ratings in a way people find intuitive and reading them in the way most people mean it.<br /> <br /> Now, could/should we work on that and make for a better general understanding of the ratings? Yes. Are the outlets a big part of this process? Yes. Do they have some fault in the situation? Yes. But more because they perpetuate a previous problem than because they created it.<br /> <br /> Companies that try to make those ratings into actual criteria for policy or benefits, like an NPS rating, that's an actual problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553501#post1553501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who knows how much acrimony there is between Paradox and the Chinese Room at this point? ... And it's all simply because these developers didn't fulfill their unrealistic expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're both easily frustrated, but stubborn on giving up. Not particularly out of any hope of success, but just to keep to their self-applied reputation of finishing things (which is also why they finished <i>Bloodlines 2</i>).<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't say their expectations are unrealistic just because they're incompetent to manage such projects. Too frequently what I get is that their expectations are unrealistic, period. Going back to my scale, an 8 is something you can reliably aim for if you have the know-how and resources, but above that isn't something even AAA projects should try on purpose with any regularity. A 9 is something you can try as a big, special project if you're really up to it, but most 9s are happy accidents as far as projects go. A 10 happens, it's a convergence of planets you can only hope to control from pure hubris.<br /> <br /> But those are the things Paradox is doing. Not accomplishing, of course, but aiming for 9 and 10, all the time, no less than 8 if they don't want to put much effort. They think they can outdo bigger companies in things even those companies only get because they make a lot of stuff, so they have more chances to get lucky. Of course, this is a very shallow simplification, but that's basically what Paradox is trying to do, when they don't have yet the resources and experience to even reliably get an 8.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. At the end everything indicates that working with them is a nightmare, and they'll throw you under the bus <b>even if you do a good job</b>, because you simply won't satisfy expectations. And they'll throw the whole project in the trash because they're frustrated, and they don't want to be seen treating a &quot;mediocre&quot; job as worthwhile.<br /> <br /> If you look carefully to the projects they actually abandoned, there are some signs that they frequently were really, <b>really</b> impossible to continue. Sure, at the same time that their frustrated post-release is basically the same as abandoning or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T06:07:36-07:00","id":1553509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553426#post1553426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire named Taylor, yes. Fabien probably would have commented on the Swift part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean Fabien <i>could </i>be a Swiftie? <br /> <br /> Imagine as part of his memories restoring... He start breaking out into Taylor Swift songs... inside the main character's mind.<br /> <br /> Or ex-prince Lou Graham and your character gushing over friendship bracelets. <br /> &quot;I'm woke up from torpor with THIS!&quot; As the PC holds up an ERAS tour friendship bracelet. <br /> <br /> One can dream of Taylor Swift x VTM BL ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T11:33:58-07:00","id":1553518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553481#post1553481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, according to this, the series of events appears to be: The Chinese Room wanted to make a VtM-game. They got approval from Paradox. They started to work on it. Then Paradox approached them and told them the game they're working on would now be called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I don\u2019t think it will change the game in the end, but this does change its initial reception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553491#post1553491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's fair. I wouldn't bet on it, but there's nothing to lose hoping for the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think hoping is a bit of a strong word for my feelings on the matter. To me, it\u2019s more like; They\u2019ve seen the backlash, they might try to fix it, or not, I\u2019m in no actual rush to buy the game.<br /> <br /> Also, they can\u2019t really do worse from that stand point, can't they?<br /> <br /> I mean, I guess corporate greed does find a way so I shouldn\u2019t jinx it, lol.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553491#post1553491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually it seems promising enough that, even if it isn't worth the full price, I think a lot of people here will just wait for a sale.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> may disagree with ratings like 6 out of 10, but that's still a game worth playing, and worth buying at <i>some</i> price.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I\u2019ve heard some decent news gamewise.<br /> <br /> Outside of actual performance issues and technical difficulties, rating has never really meant much to me.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s some game I like that I would rate pretty poorly objectively, or that I wouldn\u2019t recommend, but I still like either because I was in the mood for that game at the time, or it made me live an experience I enjoyed.<br /> <br /> Some other games I would rate highly, I don\u2019t enjoy as much on the flip side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553491#post1553491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's a fair complaint at this point, with neither of the two games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I personally, don\u2019t think it even matter in the end.<br /> <br /> I think what it invites, however, is inevitable comparisons between the two games and confusion. It tricks people into thinking it\u2019s a sequel, while it\u2019s not really the case.<br /> <br /> Hence my original statement, which I should probably have written differently :<br /> <br /> It seems like the issue a lot of people have with the game is that it\u2019s not bloodline 2.<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t think my original gut feeling of Baldur\u2019s gate 3 was fair either. My assessment of it was 100% vibe based. To me it did not feel like \u2018\u2019Baldur\u2019s gate 3\u2019\u2019, because it wasn\u2019t a sequel. I still enjoyed the game quite a bit.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, i have no issues with the fact that numerous Final Fantasy games have no easily discernible connections to each other. Probably, because I was introduced to the franchise when it was already standard for Square Enix to do so, I have no idea how the discourse surrounding the FFs was at the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T14:18:51-07:00","id":1553524,"title":"","content":"My take on the subject is that playing a vampire in the World of Darkness exploring and doing quests is enough that naming it Bloodlines isn't that big of a deal. <br /> <br /> But everyone's line in the land will be in a different place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T15:30:48-07:00","id":1553651,"title":"","content":"A little update:<br /> <br /> Paradox/Chinese Room want to address the backlash caused by the &quot;Shadow &amp; Silk&quot;-Day 1 -DLC. That's the good news. <br /> <br /> Bad news is how they've been addressing this thus far.<br /> <br /> Previously, they've announced that they were thinking about &quot;adjustments&quot;. That was <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/paradox-is-making-adjustments-to-bloodlines-2s-toreador-and-lasombra-dlc-after-the-entirely-predictable-backlash/\" target=\"_blank\">late August</a>. And I thought &quot;Yeah, sure, whatever... Just tell me the details.&quot;. Well, here where it gets bad. Things are happening - but not in any way I would have expected to be honest. Because today we got this announcement (this is a screenshot from the Discord/you can find an article about this <a href=\"https://gamerant.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-pre-order-refund/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>):<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"627\" height=\"760\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/rjcsegz.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/rjcsegz.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/rjcsegz.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> What does this mean? Who knows... But I do think it's important to still mention it because if you've pre-ordered the Premium Edition, you're about to get a refund. And then you're expected to buy the Premium Edition again (I guess) on September 17th. <br /> <br /> Regarding this whole kerfuffle, the sentiment of &quot;The best time to take action was yesterday&quot; comes to mind because that whole Day 1 DLC thing with the Clans should've been disregarded as a bad idea from the outset. But even if you were unaware of why it would turn out to be a bad decision, I didn't imagine that course-correcting would turn into yet another disaster. I mean, it can't be that outlandish to think that you only should make an announcement, once you have all your proverbial &quot;ducks in a row&quot;, right? I'm looking at this and wonder: Does the person who wrote this know what's going to be announced on September 17th? Does <i>anybody </i>know? Or are we just watching a bunch of people scrambling in a panic and nobody knows anything and then... Who even knows...<br /> <br /> Well, I guess, the game does have a release-date now. At least, I hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-05T20:53:09-07:00","id":1553658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553651#post1553651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox/Chinese Room want to address the backlash caused by the &quot;Shadow &amp; Silk&quot;-Day 1 -DLC. That's the good news.<br /> <br /> Bad news is how they've been addressing this thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost cackling here.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this didn't really surprise me. I somehow thought of the possibility of them trying to do something more complex than it actually had to be, even to the point of going back to programming and risking an all new delay on the release date. So... that's a win?<br /> <br /> At this point anything may happen. They'll probably move some pieces between the main game and the DLCs, possibly add a few easy-to-code content with AI or recycled assets. It may or may not change costs, lower if they're smart, higher if they're... well, them. A new delay may or may not happen, although they certainly hope not (they're bad at hopping things, though). It's wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T01:47:37-07:00","id":1553662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553658#post1553658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm almost cackling here.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this didn't really surprise me. I somehow thought of the possibility of them trying to do something more complex than it actually had to be, even to the point of going back to programming and risking an all new delay on the release date. So... that's a win?<br /> <br /> At this point anything may happen. They'll probably move some pieces between the main game and the DLCs, possibly add a few easy-to-code content with AI or recycled assets. It may or may not change costs, lower if they're smart, higher if they're... well, them. A new delay may or may not happen, although they certainly hope not (they're bad at hopping things, though). It's wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine being the person who already got refunded for the big premium edition once before, when the Hardsuit Labs version finally got canned. And now (still having faith in the project for some reason) you pre-ordered this Premium Edition - only to get refunded AGAIN <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !<br /> <br /> Just proves the worst thing one can do is trust Paradox.<br /> <br /> But announcing another delay on September 17th would be hilarious. &quot;The two additional Clans will be part of the base-game but the new version of the Premium-edition has different extra content - which still needs to be worked on. The new release-date will be Q1 2026!&quot; - or something like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . God, switching developers and ending up with two different versions of development-hell somehow... Now that would be an &quot;achievement&quot; for the history-books right there lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-06T14:20:41-07:00","id":1553676,"title":"","content":"Well, on the flip side they may &quot;just&quot; delay the DLC.<br /> <br /> And while it isn't impossible, I wouldn't count on them moving the two clans to the base-game. It would be sensible, but paraphrasing Lobo, &quot;they don't do logic&quot;. Doing this would arguably augment the base-game's value (without re-pricing it) while reducing the DLC's value (without cashing on it).<br /> <br /> Think about it. The problem was the Day-1 DLC. If the DLC isn't Day-1, problem solved. The worse that can happen now is for this DLC to not only be delayed, but also get even pricier with very little actual improvement.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I think the worse will happen. I simply don't know. They may add superfluous content and delay the DLC a few days, they may add actually more clans to it and delay its release for quite some time, but still deliver the base-game in time, they may indeed move one or both clans to the base-game, at this point anything goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-08T21:00:58-07:00","id":1553699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553499#post1553499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, I'm a very forgiving reviewer, but I tend to view 6 out of 10 as, &quot;BARELY worth playing at any price&quot;<br /> <br /> 8 out of 10 is more, &quot;I liked it&quot;<br /> <br /> While 9 out of 10 and 10 out of 10 is &quot;I loved it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other people believe the latter must be perfect games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the big issue with the 1-10 scale is that you see people use it based on two different ideas. The first is the US grading scale where any grade below 7 (70%) is a failure and 8 (80%) is considered average. On that scale a 7/10 is barely passable and not worth purchasing at full price.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you have people grading where a 5 (50%) means average so a 7 means the game is actually rather above average and should be pretty solid.<br /> <br /> The problem is, you don't always know which grading scale someone is using. That's why I prefer a 1-5 system. Everyone understands a 3 is fairly average, so a 3 and a half (which would be 7/10 on the other scale) is more understood to be above average rather than barely acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-09-2025, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-09T14:30:36-07:00","id":1553719,"title":"","content":"I'm going to place a bet for the Day-1 DLC will be free but they'll add something paid in its place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T19:13:44-07:00","id":1553802,"title":"","content":"Not really anything too new...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/bloodlines-2-narrative-director-tries-to-get-players-to-lower-their-expectations-patiently-explains-its-not-going-to-have-the-scale-of-baldurs-gate-3-or-grand-theft-auto/\" target=\"_blank\">PC Gamer</a> - <b>Bloodlines 2 narrative director tries to get players to lower their expectations</b><br /> <br /> While we will get to choose the clan and gender of our player-character in Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2, it's apparently not going to be a full &quot;how many skill points do I want to put into Security&quot; kind of character creation\u2014a revelation that's set a few fans on edge. Narrative director Ian Thomas put in some damage control by explaining that decision to PCGamesN, which I'm sure White Wolf tragics will give calm and reasonable consideration to.<br /> <br /> Elaborating on why the player-character in Bloodlines 2 isn't the typical RPG &quot;blank slate&quot;, Thomas said, &quot;if you're telling a specific story, I think you need a shape to pour the story into, like a mold. If you completely open up all of the options and throw somebody into a space, how do you make that character the pillar of the story?&quot;<br /> <br /> And Bloodlines 2 will be telling a very specific story. Comparing it to Baldur's Gate 3, which does let you go full blank-slate and wander off-piste between plot points, Thomas put the two philosophies into tabletop RPG terms. &quot;For me Baldur's Gate 3 is writing an entire roleplaying setting, whereas what we've done is write a roleplaying module,&quot; he said, suggesting Bloodlines 2 will be more about telling a singular one-and-done story than opening up a map and letting you have at it.<br /> <br /> The original Bloodlines, while smaller than Baldur's Gate 3, did give you fairly free rein across its open hubs, with plenty of side missions to explore as you saw fit. Bloodlines 2, with its customizable yet defined protagonist and pre-set scenario, seems like it's aiming for something different, and you can see why the developers at The Chinese Room are eager to manage our expectations.<br /> <br /> As Thomas says, &quot;It does make it hard when people see [Bloodlines 2] and go 'oh I thought this was an entire setting, I thought this was GTA where we could do anything!' While we're trying to go 'no, it's this slice of time and place.'&quot;<br /> <br /> We'll be able to see how that choice pays off for ourselves when Bloodlines 2 releases on October 21. </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T20:23:15-07:00","id":1553807,"title":"","content":"&quot;...which I'm sure White Wolf tragics will give calm and reasonable consideration to.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wow that's some... questionable editorial decisions by PC Gamer there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T00:29:36-07:00","id":1553810,"title":"","content":"What a bizarre response... But I think it's important to see it in the context of the original article in PCGamesN, titled <a href=\"https://www.pcgamesn.com/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/baldurs-gate-3-pressure\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;If Baldur's Gate 3 is &quot;an entire roleplay setting,&quot; Bloodlines 2 is a &quot;scenario&quot; &quot;</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's now 2025 and Larian's set the bar exceedingly high. With the specter of the first game forever looming, I ask if BG3's success has made Bloodlines 2's development harder.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think it's fair to say that it has,&quot; narrative director Ian Thomas tells me. &quot;There's that feeling that we should be able to open [things up] and customize [everything from a] completely blank slate. But if you're telling a specific story, I think you need a shape to pour the story into, like a mold. If you completely open up all of the options and throw somebody into a space, how do you make that character the pillar of the story?&quot;<br /> <br /> By contrast, Bloodlines 2 is a more focused RPG: the city has clear boundaries, not every NPC is interactable, and you can't (at least in my experience) yeet a vampire off of the side of a cliff mid-boss fight by throwing rats at him (thanks, Lua). &quot;For me Baldur's Gate 3 is writing an entire roleplaying setting, whereas what we've done is write a roleplaying module,&quot; he says, promptly sparking a debate about whether the term is 'module,' 'adventure,' or 'scenario' (White Wolf's World of Darkness band manager Jason Carl seems pretty set on scenario). <br /> <br /> &quot;It does make it hard when people see [Bloodlines 2] and go 'oh I thought this was an entire setting, I thought this was GTA where we could do anything!' While we're trying to go 'no, it's this slice of time and place.'&quot; <br /> <br /> While the idea of a Baldur's Gate 3-scale Vampire: The Masquerade game is certainly appealing, the original Bloodlines was a relatively self-contained, mission-based game, taking you from A (for Ankaran Sarcophagus) to B (for Beckett or bloody demise - you choose) with side-quests along the way. A fully open-world VTM RPG could be amazing, sure, but Bloodlines 2's linearity feels more in-line (pun intended) with the original game. But, a girl can certainly dream. </div> </div> </div>First of all, insane premise to start an interview with &quot;Did the success of Baldurs Gate 3 make development harder for you?&quot;. It's even worse, though, to take that premise seriously in their response. That section there just comes off as Ian whining about the success of BG3. Other roleplaying-games have come out since Baldurs Gate 3 left early access. Should every Metroidvania game-developer in the foreseeable future come out and complain about the success of Hollow Knight: Silksong as well while we're at it? That's ridiculous. <br /> <br /> Besides, they should just explain what the actual game is like. Instead of whining about big and successful games of the past that are not like Bloddlines 2, they should simply explain what the game's like. Better yet, rather than explaining, show off more comprehensive gameplay-examples. Like showing off what you can do in combat when you're mid-game and you have acess to powers from multiple Clans or show off a section where dialogue-choices had an impact on the story... Unless it's one of those linear games where only towards the end you get a choice that determines whether you get Ending A or Ending B and outside of that the story can't be changed (and/or maybe there's a secret ending if you have all the collectibles or something). And the way &quot;linearity&quot; keeps coming up when they talk about what the game is actually like, I really have a suspicion that this is the type of game we're looking at here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T02:02:50-07:00","id":1553811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553810#post1553810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better yet, rather than explaining, show off more comprehensive gameplay-examples. Like showing off what you can do in combat when you're mid-game and you have acess to powers from multiple Clans or show off a section where dialogue-choices had an impact on the story... Unless it's one of those linear games where only towards the end you get a choice that determines whether you get Ending A or Ending B and outside of that the story can't be changed (and/or maybe there's a secret ending if you have all the collectibles or something). And the way &quot;linearity&quot; keeps coming up when they talk about what the game is actually like, I really have a suspicion that this is the type of game we're looking at here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect they don't want to show off too much gameplay because the game doesn't look or play very well. From what little we have seen, the NPCs were not looking too great. There's probably a risk that if they show off a lot of gameplay people will decide Bloodlines 2 is not a $60 game and will cancel preorders. So by sticking to using verbal interviews they can try and temper opinions before the game comes out so that people expect that it went be great, while making it less likely that it will turn people away from the game. <br /> <br /> That said, I do think the BG3 question is reasonable. BG3 has left a massive footprint on the CRPG genre and managed to go mainstream in a way RPGs rarely do. There are a lot of people for whom BG3 is the first RPG they've played, and it may have given them unreasonable expectations when it comes to the genre. I've been seeing similar questions asked of JRPG designers concerning Expedition 33, which has had a somewhat similar impact for that genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T06:14:13-07:00","id":1553814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553811#post1553811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect they don't want to show off too much gameplay because the game doesn't look or play very well. From what little we have seen, the NPCs were not looking too great. There's probably a risk that if they show off a lot of gameplay people will decide Bloodlines 2 is not a $60 game and will cancel preorders. So by sticking to using verbal interviews they can try and temper opinions before the game comes out so that people expect that it went be great, while making it less likely that it will turn people away from the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are any shortcomings regarding performance or if there's like a big drop in quality in terms of writing, visuals and combat (for example, things getting repetitive) towards the end, then the Day 1 DLC will hit twice as hard. Because then you gotta wonder how they had found the time to develop those two extra playable Clans (that then could be sold at a premium price) but somehow there wasn't room to address any such problems like performance, stiff facial animations etc.<br /> <br /> And I guess, now it depends on what they decide to announce on the 17th. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553811#post1553811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I do think the BG3 question is reasonable. BG3 has left a massive footprint on the CRPG genre and managed to go mainstream in a way RPGs rarely do. There are a lot of people for whom BG3 is the first RPG they've played, and it may have given them unreasonable expectations when it comes to the genre. I've been seeing similar questions asked of JRPG designers concerning Expedition 33, which has had a somewhat similar impact for that genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Clair, I get why you would bring it up. Considering how great the critical reception has been, it's certainly a game of the year contender and so with that reputation in mind, it isn't surprising people are wondering how it stacks up against Baldurs Gate 3. And then it's interesting to wonder how the developers feel about people comparing Clair Obscura with BG3.<br /> <br /> In the case of Bloodlines 2, though, I don't think the existence of BG3 matters all that much. Or the existence of GTA. I mean, there was a time when GTA 6 was slated to release this year. If there are any misapprehensions about what the game is or isn't like, I think there are a couple of factors at play here that weigh far heavier than people thinking of BG3.<ul><li>First, the game's called Bloodlines 2. And so it's normal to expect something similar to Bloodlines 1.</li> <li>Second, the game's price-range is 60 to 90 $. And so people will look around at what other games of the same genre and at that price-point are around.</li> <li>Third, the game's been in development-hell for many years. People have tuned out, pay less attention and are less interested in what's going on with the game.</li> <li>Fourth, they haven't done enough to give people a proper impression of what the game's like.</li> </ul>I feel like all four of these points work against them. More importantly, Paradox/Chinese Room has control over these. This game didn't have to be called Bloodlines 2. The price-range didn't have to be that high. They could've cut their losses instead of insisting on a release. They can't do anything, though, about the fact that BG3 exists.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't help that even when they talk to the press, it isn't great PR. I don't think it helps that when they talk, you get phrases like &quot;lowering expectations&quot;, &quot;damage control&quot;, &quot;It does make it hard!&quot;, &quot;linear&quot;, &quot;It's not a setting, it's a scenario&quot; etc. The game's not even out yet and it already feels like we're halfway to this being an apology-tour. <br /> <br /> The best-case scenario would be for them to be able to show off the game and present a pitch of why it's cool and you should wanna buy the game to experience this. And if they can't, they should just not say anything. Just release the game. It sucks but it is what it is. But this... Sure, there may be people who don't have a lot of experience with RPGs maybe and since BG3 is their only experience with it but what's the point of going out there and say &quot;Please don't think this is like BG3. It's worse.&quot; How is that supposed to help? The Day 1 DLC thing didn't help as well or how even the Chinese Room version had been delayed two times... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T15:02:54-07:00","id":1553818,"title":"","content":"I don't think the questions about BG3 or GTA6 are about the specifics of those franchises, but rather how franchises have evolved since Bloodlines 1 came out. GTA is basically the current king of open world gaming and has come a huge way from where it started. The BG series is more to the point as both the resurrection of an older dormant franchise, an adaptation of a TTRPG, and something that didn't come from a major &quot;AAA&quot; studio (they were basically just the <i>Divinity</i> series studio until BG3 happened). It's not &quot;we're expecting BL2 to be as expansive as GTA6, or adapt the fantasy tropes and mechanics of BG3, why is that not happening?&quot; but rather, &quot;Given the success of BG3 in resurrecting an older TTRPG based property and the kind of experiences we're expecting out of GTA6, how is that going to meet the expectations of a sequel to Bloodlines 1?&quot;<br /> <br /> I agree the &quot;journalism&quot; on display in these articles is unfair in it's framing, but the point they seem to be getting at isn't so far off from points 1, 2, and 4 above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T19:01:25-07:00","id":1553823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553810#post1553810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, insane premise to start an interview with &quot;Did the success of Baldurs Gate 3 make development harder for you?&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question was horrible. The game is not this kind of RPG, and is not a continuation to this kind of RPG. Even a better PR person wouldn't be able to answer much better than &quot;this is not that type of game&quot;. Heck, the last paragraph make it clear that the interviewer asked this simply because she wanted another game and that's it. Yeah, a girl can dream, but a professional shouldn't act on a pointless dream with no root on reality. She ended up kind of setting up the interviewed to a bad response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553810#post1553810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, they should just explain what the actual game is like. Instead of whining about big and successful games of the past that are not like Bloddlines 2, they should simply explain what the game's like.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that Paradox, not necessarily The Chinese Room, is locked in the thought of keeping everything a secret until the release, just because that's how you do. So I'm not sure they can do much about it.<br /> <br /> I do worry about just how linear it will be. I'm mostly accepting that it will be linear as hell and anything less is an improvement. More importantly, linearity doesn't necessarily means a bad game.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think anything they said is an indication in this direction because their spiel is already tainted by the now well established defeatist stance they have on this game. Add to that how the question was phrased, what do you say about linearity when you're being asked to compare with BG3? <b>Of course it's linear, it isn't BG3</b>.<br /> <br /> We already know they're assuming the worse without reason and they're bad at PR. The answer given don't really add any new information.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553814#post1553814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like all four of these points work against them. More importantly, Paradox/Chinese Room has control over these. This game didn't have to be called Bloodlines 2. The price-range didn't have to be that high. They could've cut their losses instead of insisting on a release. They can't do anything, though, about the fact that BG3 exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's precisely why they'll chose to blame Baldur's Gate 3. As they can't do anything about it, it isn't something they did wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T21:22:30-07:00","id":1553830,"title":"","content":"Everything else, aside, I think Ian Thomas' response to the BG3 question was really bad.<br /> <br /> He should have said something along the lines of, &quot;RPGs aren't monolithic. Some of them like BG3 focus on narrative freedom. Others, like Telltale's The Walking Dead are more scenario driven. Whether a game has a lot of narrative freedom or if it sacrifices some of that freedom to tell a tighter story, one isn't necessarily better than the other. People can come away from both styles of RPGs feeling satisfied with what they played. As for Bloodlines 2, it's going to be much more scenario focused and we hope people enjoy the story we have to tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that would have felt more like setting expectations up rather than downplaying people's expectations. I came away feeling like Ian Thomas is bad at giving interviews, or he doesn't have a whole lot of faith in his product, or possibly both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T09:42:53-07:00","id":1553876,"title":"","content":"Here's the promised announcement about the changes (<a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/game-overview\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2: Lasombra and Toreador clans are confirmed for the base game at launch, making all 6 clans playable for everyone!<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks to our community for the frank feedback on Bloodlines 2 and the Premium Edition. That feedback made it clear: Lasombra and Toreador belong in the base game, so that is what we are doing,&quot; said Marco Behrmann, White Wolf Executive Vice President and Bloodlines 2 Executive Producer.<br /> <br /> &quot;We\u2019d also like to thank The Chinese Room for their quick turnaround on the concepts for the post-launch Story Packs. We\u2019re constantly impressed by their creativity and skill in weaving enticing narrative threads that expand on the main story in Bloodlines 2.&quot;<br /> <br /> We\u2019re also unveiling two new Bloodlines 2 Story Packs: \u201cLoose Cannon\u201c (Brujah Sheriff Benny\u2019s story) and \u201cThe Flower &amp; The Flame\u201d (Toreador Primogen Ysabella\u2019s path). Both are included in the Premium Edition Expansion Pass, alongside the day one unlock Santa Monica Memories Cosmetic Pack, and will be released in 2026.<br /> <br /> Digital Editions<ul><li>Bloodlines 2 Deluxe Edition: Base game + Santa Monica Memories cosmetic pack</li> <li>Bloodlines 2 Premium Edition: Base game + Expansion Pass (Santa Monica Memories, Loose Cannon, The Flower &amp; The Flame)</li> </ul><br /> Physical Editions<ul><li>Day One Edition: Base game + Bloodlines Nostalgia Jukebox bonus. Select retailers will also have a physical cross necklace inspired by the Cross of St. James.</li> <li>Premium Edition: Base Game, Nostalgia Jukebox pre-order bonus, the Expansion Pass, five character cards, a journal, and a Steelbook case, packaged in a premium box (limited quantities!)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Story Pack Release Dates<ul><li>Loose Cannon (Q2 2026) - Brujah Sheriff Benny\u2019s story + Benny outfit for Phyre</li> <li>The Flower &amp; The Flame (Q3 2026) - Toreador Primogen Ysabella\u2019s path + Ysabella outfit for Phyre</li> </ul><br /> The action-RPG video game is the sequel to the cult classic Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines. Vampire: the Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 lets players step into its story through two distinct, alternating perspectives: Elder vampire Phyre and Malkavian detective Fabien. </div> </div> </div>Overall, a good change. And quite a big one considering how Paradox's leadership talked about the game last year. And good for the Chinese Room, now that they're independent again, that this means Paradox will be paying them to work on the game post-launch to create the story-DLCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T13:11:16-07:00","id":1553882,"title":"","content":"Yay for the fact the two clans are part of the Base GameTM.<br /> <br /> But I don't blame Paradox in the slightest for ONE thing and that is keeping so much of this under wraps until a month before release. We won't know the story for another decade probably but I think already the story is that Hardsuit Labs was massively behind schedule for a variety of reasons and had only managed to make the section of the game we played plus other assets. This is why the Chinese Room, despite the fact they had access to all of Hardsuit Labs and had no problem using them, more or less had to start from scratch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T16:58:27-07:00","id":1553886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553876#post1553876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, a good change. And quite a big one considering how Paradox's leadership talked about the game last year. And good for the Chinese Room, now that they're independent again, that this means Paradox will be paying them to work on the game post-launch to create the story-DLCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That's almost out-of-character for them, but it's definitely good news!<br /> <br /> Color me impressed, I really didn't expect them to do the most sensible decision, but they did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553882#post1553882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't blame Paradox in the slightest for ONE thing and that is keeping so much of this under wraps until a month before release.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is such a mystery. They straight up said it up when they revealed they were working with The Chinese Room: they were going to scrap the project, TCR made a new pitch.<br /> <br /> You're a writer, how would it be if something similar happened with you? You have the basic premise of a book, but the original author won't finish it anymore. You want to work with the idea and they let you use everything they already have written. Does it really maters if they have just a little or a lot of the work done? Making a video game is very different, but not in this regard. In this, it's almost identical.<br /> <br /> What made this viable to begin with is that TCR wasn't asked to just finish the original project. They did their thing. Under such circumstances, how much work was already done is irrelevant, it wasn't their project, and fortunately they received the green light to make their own project. The alternative would be something like the first Super Mario Bros movie.<br /> <br /> All that said... why give more details? That'll just serve to bash Hardsuit Labs. It's probably a breach of contract and possibly even ilegal as it would expose people for no good reason. We are used as public to demand information and sometimes get whistleblowers, but actually that's not how things work. There are things we have no place knowing about, at least until it becomes history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T01:42:01-07:00","id":1553895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553886#post1553886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. That's almost out-of-character for them, but it's definitely good news!<br /> <br /> Color me impressed, I really didn't expect them to do the most sensible decision, but they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Although it has to be said, that yes, on one hand this was a good decision. But on the other hand, Paradox had to be dragged there. And that goes to show how important it is in situations like this to voice criticism and not hold back. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1553886#post1553886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is such a mystery. They straight up said it up when they revealed they were working with The Chinese Room: they were going to scrap the project, TCR made a new pitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also switched engines for the TCR game. I don't remember what engine Hardsuit Labs were using but I do remember TCR talking about their decision to switch to Unreal 5. So they couldn't simply &quot;continue&quot; what Hardsuit Labs were doing. It's really more accurate to think of the Hardsuit Labs game and the TCR game as two different games considering how different they were conceptually and how they were made.<br /> <br /> Just as an aside, I wonder if the Unreal 5 problems will come up here as well. Now with Borderlands 4 there has been some talk about how tricky Unreal 5 can be when it comes to optimization which then leads to performance issues. I mean, the system requirements they posted for Bloodlines 2 look moderate so it doesn't seem badly optimized but I guess we'll see if any issues with Bloodlines 2 will make it part of this conversation about the Unreal 5 engine. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T11:56:56-07:00","id":1553908,"title":"","content":"A TTRPG player and UE5 programmer I know once said of UE5 that it's a lot like GURPS: if you can do everything you need to do with the core book and maybe one or two supplements? It's actually a really smooth system and runs well. The problems are when you're ten supplements in to run all the different pieces you want to include, because that's when the complexity starts overloading bandwidth. For GURPS, that's mental bandwidth, for video games that's processing power (mostly CPU and GPU).<br /> <br /> Optimization helps, but it's a lot of cost for the effort. UE5 isn't friendly towards code optimization, but there's a lot of people that are skilled at it if you're willing to pay them so.. that's a thing. There's also the increasing issues that are coming out of the end of the Console Wars. With Sony and Microsoft basically ceasing with console exclusives, most big video games need to run on multiple platforms, which amplifies the problem. Microsoft trying to become the Netflix of video games is another issue because the more people playing on the Game Pass cloud servers, the more giant corporate servers are running the games and optimization doesn't really matter; badly optimized games run great if you're a subscriber, which is another way to squeeze you for money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T16:02:26-07:00","id":1554276,"title":"","content":"Another trailer up, this time looking at Clan Lasombra, which is what I was the most curious about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AZV_stoD20\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AZV_stoD20\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AZV_stoD20\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AZV_stoD20 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it seems like Phyre was part of the Sabbat before going into Topor and then waking up and joining the Camarilla seems to be a part of their story. That's kind of cool. I admit, I did smirk at the &quot;stupid fucking name&quot; part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T16:50:16-07:00","id":1554278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554276#post1554276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it seems like Phyre was part of the Sabbat before going into Topor and then waking up and joining the Camarilla seems to be a part of their story. That's kind of cool. I admit, I did smirk at the &quot;stupid fucking name&quot; part.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big sign that Chinese Room &quot;gets&quot; it is that all of these NPCs have immense snarky attitudes and reactions based on your clothing or Clan.<br /> <br /> This seems like a much more option filled game than people suspected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-16T22:54:51-07:00","id":1554399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554278#post1554278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A big sign that Chinese Room &quot;gets&quot; it is that all of these NPCs have immense snarky attitudes and reactions based on your clothing or Clan.<br /> <br /> This seems like a much more option filled game than people suspected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect it'll be dialogue flavour more than anything. Its unlikely bloodlines will have fully fleshed out alternative paths with clans. Im a 99% that being ex sabbat will not be reflected in any way narratively (explicitly in ideological opposition to the tower and the movement) or mechanically (you're not going to be on a path for example).<br /> <br /> <br /> Its a nice nod but I think its a good idea not to get expectations too high. Which is how im approaching the game in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T02:05:22-07:00","id":1554404,"title":"","content":"Let's be honest that true alternative paths aren't really that common a thing.<br /> <br /> For most games &quot;not linear&quot; just means you can wander through an area that's bigger than the main quest needs it to be, so you have unimportant things to do, but the events (even side quests) are still scripted with very little or no variation. Even when you have actual alternate paths, most of the time they'll lead you to the same points sooner or later, and endings rarely take into account many details of your journey.<br /> <br /> So while the game may be far more &quot;linear&quot; than we would want, let's not pretend what we want is a lot. Dialogue flavor is the main kind of alternate path anyways. If we keep too focused on this, we may end up being harsher on the linearity than the game actually deserves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T02:27:36-07:00","id":1554405,"title":"","content":"I've been watching the Clan Trailers and... Well, first of all, when I saw the &quot;Blink&quot;-ability for Toreador, I laughed out loud because you couldn't make the Dishonored-inspiration more obvious. <br /> <br /> But regarding choices, the thing I've been wondering about is that you get these snippets in the Clan-Trailers where it seems the Phyre-voice-actors do give their line-readings a bit of Clan-specific verve. But I doubt this game had the budget/time where the voice-actors did Clan-specific line-readings from beginning to end. I'm sure with good enough voice-actors, you technically could do that but, well... we know what development has been like for this game. Rather, as previously shown, I imagine, you simply occasionally get the option to give a &quot;Clan-flavored&quot; response. But that's the only time when the Clan-specific character of the voice-performance will come out. I wonder if it will create some incongruity when you contrast a Toreador-answer with the neutral voice-performance you get most of the time with Phyre otherwise, for example. <br /> <br /> As for linearity... I still think one shouldn't expect too much. Nothing in the previews indicated we're about to get some sprawling tapestry of different endings. My impression is more of this being a mix of Dishonored-lite and Mass-Effect-lite mechanics. Therefore, ending-wise, I would guess it's one of those where you get a slide-show at the end and overall you have a good ending, a bad one and a true one and then some added flavor a la &quot;Did you side with the Anarchists or the Camarilla?&quot; where you get different slides depending on obvious binary choices like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T08:36:37-07:00","id":1554421,"title":"","content":"Looks like reviews are coming in. Generally it seems to be scoring in the 5-7 range with a few outliers that are really bad. The really bad reviews seem to have run into game-ruining bugs, but these seem to be relatively rare. Most of the cons on the game are that the combat is not much fun and the game is very on-the-rails and linear. People also don't seem to like how much walking you have to do, retreading back and forth across the maps multiple times to carry out fetch quests.<br /> <br /> Overall the biggest knock seems to be from people simply saying that the game is not a worthy successor to the first Bloodlines. I think if the game hadn't called itself Bloodlines 2 reviewers would have been a bit more gentle with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T09:18:57-07:00","id":1554423,"title":"","content":"Yeah, been reading some reviews and... it's kinda what I expected it to be. Also, I read that the game-map is pretty small and feels a bit sterile. I mean, considering what we know of the development, nothing the reviews mention is too surprising. And if one paid close attention to the previews and read between the lines, then the shortcomings were pretty clear. Well, at least they made the right call of reversing the decision with the Day 1 DLC and locking two Clans behind a paywall. <br /> <br /> Game-breaking bugs, though... Uff, well, hopefully the paying customers will benefit from a Day 1 Patch that addresses at least some of those. It's a full-price game, after all.<br /> <br /> I'm still thinking about whether to get it or not... But the way the reviews sound, this seems more like one you should get during a future sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T11:15:41-07:00","id":1554425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554399#post1554399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect it'll be dialogue flavour more than anything. Its unlikely bloodlines will have fully fleshed out alternative paths with clans. Im a 99% that being ex sabbat will not be reflected in any way narratively (explicitly in ideological opposition to the tower and the movement) or mechanically (you're not going to be on a path for example).<br /> <br /> <br /> Its a nice nod but I think its a good idea not to get expectations too high. Which is how im approaching the game in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why we should expect the Sabbat to be a thing either as the Sabbat path of Bloodlines is purely a fan creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554421#post1554421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall the biggest knock seems to be from people simply saying that the game is not a worthy successor to the first Bloodlines. I think if the game hadn't called itself Bloodlines 2 reviewers would have been a bit more gentle with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think that if it hadn't done it, it would have never gotten any attention whatsoever and people would be wondering why it wasn't called Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T11:56:34-07:00","id":1554427,"title":"","content":"I think it's mostly Paradox's fault that the comparison to Bloodlines 1 is being made. It isn't just the name, it's part of what Paradox wants people to think about. When Bloodlines 2 was originally announced they even had brought on people who had worked on BL1 after all. And even with the Chinese Room going into a very different direction, you still have the cosmetic pack called &quot;Santa Monica Memories&quot; where it says <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 - Santa Monica Memories lets you relive the nostalgia of the original Bloodlines. To decorate your haven, this cosmetic pack features iconic items, including a Stop Sign, Ankaran Sarcophagus, and Voerman Portrait. Additionally, with Santa Monica Memories, your haven will be adorned with a clan neon sign each time you complete the game as a new clan. </div> </div> </div>So it isn't like the marketing doesn't want people to think about Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, it's not like anybody was forcing Paradox to release a sequel to Bloodlines. Obviously, with BL1 having a cult-following there were quite a lot of people wishing for a sequel. But still, it was a choice by Paradox to deal with the expectations and demands that come with finally announcing that anticipated sequel. Additionally, the way this had turned into this lengthy and troubled odyssey was wholly unrelated to it being called Bloodlines 2. <br /> <br /> It also doesn't help that I've played Hollow Knight: Silksong and Hades 2 this year. These are two great games and they're great examples of sequels done right. Both games took everything from their predecessor and just gave you even more. These are sequels done the right way. Of course, there are a lot of differences between these games. But if we're just sticking with the idea of a sequel: When you're putting a game in front of me called Bloodlines 2, the game better be able to make the case of why it's called that. And having played two games this year that are well-made examples that this can be done leads to the Bloodlines-name become a drawback for this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T13:35:36-07:00","id":1554429,"title":"","content":"Heres the thing....it looks a LOT like Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I think of atmosphere, sense of humor, and storytelling for Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Not game mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T14:33:41-07:00","id":1554430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554429#post1554429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heres the thing....it looks a LOT like Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I think of atmosphere, sense of humor, and storytelling for Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Not game mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, aside from the generational upgrade to graphics, of course, which leads to visual differences.<br /> <br /> And game-mechanics are a pretty big deal. What you're describing is so broad that at that point, you could release a movie named Bloodlines 2 and call it a day. I would hazard a guess that for most fans of BL1, they'd wish for a sequel to take the game-mechanics and develop/expand them. Because the roleplaying game-mechanics are part of what people love about BL1. That's a huge part of what made it appealing as a game. And it's why the critical sequel-talk has found so much resonance in discussions about Bloodlines 2. You're ignoring the elephant in the room if you're not talking about the huge game-mechanic-differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T15:14:23-07:00","id":1554432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554430#post1554430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, aside from the generational upgrade to graphics, of course, which leads to visual differences.<br /> <br /> And game-mechanics are a pretty big deal. What you're describing is so broad that at that point, you could release a movie named Bloodlines 2 and call it a day. I would hazard a guess that for most fans of BL1, they'd wish for a sequel to take the game-mechanics and develop/expand them. Because the roleplaying game-mechanics are part of what people love about BL1. That's a huge part of what made it appealing as a game. And it's why the critical sequel-talk has found so much resonance in discussions about Bloodlines 2. You're ignoring the elephant in the room if you're not talking about the huge game-mechanic-differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it?<br /> <br /> Because this argument would apply from Dragon Age: Origins to Dragon Age 2, Fallout: New Vegas to Fallout 4, and Oblivion to Skyrim<br /> <br /> In fact they're almost all about switching from large complex systems to much more streamlined ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T15:31:43-07:00","id":1554434,"title":"","content":"To be honest I abandoned Fallout as soon as they abandoned it's original system. And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Knightingale</a>'s point is about Bloodlines, not about any franchise. The system, and how open it was to build a character and see the effects of your choices, was a big deal with the (late) success of the game.<br /> <br /> But that said, I overall agree that all things considered, this is Bloodlines 2. It is not the BL 2 we wanted, it can't hold a candle to the original, but it's still Bloodlines 2. There's no point in beating this dead horse, doing a BL sequel was the whole point, and as bad as it is it was delivered. And I don't think it's a mistake on their part (despite many <i>other</i> mistakes on their part), the point of a sequel is not to live up to the original, as much as this is desired.<br /> <br /> Overall it seems the results are good. The game isn't worth the full price, but definitely worth a sale. Lets wait and see if the bugs are corrected, if it happens before a full month I wouldn't say it's a terrible thing (surely a problem for their sales, but within reasonable expectations for me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T17:04:38-07:00","id":1554437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554434#post1554434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I abandoned Fallout as soon as they abandoned it's original system. And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Knightingale</a>'s point is about Bloodlines, not about any franchise. The system, and how open it was to build a character and see the effects of your choices, was a big deal with the (late) success of the game.<br /> <br /> <b>But that said, I overall agree that all things considered, this is Bloodlines 2. It is not the BL 2 we wanted, it can't hold a candle to the original, but it's still Bloodlines 2. There's no point in beating this dead horse, doing a BL sequel was the whole point, and as bad as it is it was delivered. And I don't think it's a mistake on their part (despite many <i>other</i> mistakes on their part), the point of a sequel is not to live up to the original, as much as this is desired.</b><br /> <br /> Overall it seems the results are good. <b>The game isn't worth the full price, but definitely worth a sale. </b>Lets wait and see if the bugs are corrected, if it happens before a full month I wouldn't say it's a terrible thing (surely a problem for their sales, but within reasonable expectations for me).</div> </div> </div> </div>With respect, maybe we can play the game before we make sweeping judgements like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T21:06:41-07:00","id":1554442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554437#post1554437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With respect, maybe we can play the game before we make sweeping judgements like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, I'm talking based on what was said by others. On the other hand, the opinion of other people is the only thing I have to rely upon before deciding if it's worth my money.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking something I definitely know, but I'm not talking from complete ignorance either, and I'm literally comparing it to Bloodlines. What's the fucking problem with not being as good as <i>Bloodlines</i>!? It's like saying a movie isn't as good as <i>The Godfather</i> or <i>Citizen Kane</i>, or a book can't hold a candle to <i>The Lord of the Rings</i>, a comic didn't live up to <i>Watchmen</i>. I literally said it isn't as good compared to an extremely high bar, and I stand to it, I pretty much doubt this game has any chance to be as good as people would expect if they base this expectation on <i>Bloodlines</i>.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I stand to what I said. And given it's price tag, that's another high (although not so high) bar, it's a ridiculous price unless this game delivers far, far above its promise in every regard. I don't casually spend such money on a single game I'm not sure I'll like, this is for my most desired titles.<br /> <br /> This is a game, not a person, and a game we've been discussing all this time and now seen the first reviews. I pretty much am in my right to make sweeping judgement, especially as it is in continuation to seven pages of discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T02:24:08-07:00","id":1554443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554442#post1554442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And given it's price tag, that's another high (although not so high) bar, it's a ridiculous price unless this game delivers far, far above its promise in every regard. I don't casually spend such money on a single game I'm not sure I'll like, this is for my most desired titles.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the general opinion of the reviews I've seen <br /> <br /> &quot;It's not as good as Bloodlines 1. It's not a bad game, it's not a good game, it's an acceptable game. It's not worth $60-$70, and if you spend that much you'll probably be frustrated. Grab it when it's on sale for $30-$40, it's worth about that much.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T04:38:03-07:00","id":1554444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554432#post1554432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it?<br /> <br /> Because this argument would apply from Dragon Age: Origins to Dragon Age 2, Fallout: New Vegas to Fallout 4, and Oblivion to Skyrim<br /> <br /> In fact they're almost all about switching from large complex systems to much more streamlined ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think with Bethesda games (Fallout and Elder Scrolls), you have a pretty strong throughline. Going from Morrowind to Skyrim or Fallout 3 to Fallout 4 isn't any kind of drastic shift similar to what's happening with Bloodlines 2 here. After all, we're talking about the switch from a fullblown RPG to an action-adventure with barely any RPG-elements.<br /> <br /> Dragon Age, on the other hand, though... Yeah, comparing gameplay of Origins to what you get in Veilguard is a pretty drastic shift. Not just in terms of mechanics but also in terms of the visual style. But Dragon Age is also a great example of a mishandled franchise. That's why, even three games later when Veilguard came out, the one Dragon Age game that was fondly remembered was the first one, Dragon Age: Origins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554443#post1554443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to be the general opinion of the reviews I've seen<br /> <br /> &quot;It's not as good as Bloodlines 1. It's not a bad game, it's not a good game, it's an acceptable game. It's not worth $60-$70, and if you spend that much you'll probably be frustrated. Grab it when it's on sale for $30-$40, it's worth about that much.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My take-away from the reviews has been that the main-story seems to begreat but everything else in the game is awkward or feels unpolished. That and the game-length being on the shorter side with 20 to 30 hours (depending on how many side-stuff you do) really got me to think this is one for a future sale.<br /> <br /> Also, when I read something like this in the <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-review/\" target=\"_blank\">PC Gamer review</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two thirds of the way through the game, I'd unlocked every clan power, every clan outfit and had a loadout that had been working for me for 20 hours. So I started skipping the side stuff. As a completionist, this is not normal for me, but I hate having my time wasted.<br /> <br /> It just seems like The Chinese Room felt it had to include sidequests, so it threw a series of incredibly low-effort ones into the mix. The same goes for the open world. Nighttime Seattle is dense in atmosphere and at times incredibly striking, but there's hardly anything to do in the city. I almost feel bad for complaining about open world bloat now, because if this is the alternative? Well, no thanks.<br /> <br /> Anything not related to the main quest is simply not great. And that's a significant problem in an RPG\u2014even one as brisk as this. And while the main quest has much to recommend it, it's not quite exceptional enough to completely make up for the poor quality of Bloodlines 2's meagre side activities. The writing elevates the critical path, but there isn't anything that will stick in my mind like Bloodlines 1's terrifying Ocean House Hotel or Death Mask Productions. </div> </div> </div>Considering this is a full-priced game, that sounds rough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T04:39:59-07:00","id":1554445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554443#post1554443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to be the general opinion of the reviews I've seen<br /> <br /> &quot;It's not as good as Bloodlines 1. It's not a bad game, it's not a good game, it's an acceptable game. It's not worth $60-$70, and if you spend that much you'll probably be frustrated. Grab it when it's on sale for $30-$40, it's worth about that much.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats my spin. Its not as good as bloodlines which i bought for 20 quid back in the day. Plus its gonna have dlc. Im gonna wait until steam summer sale at least.<br /> <br /> Edit plus i proactively dislike paradox as a company so dont like giving them money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-18-2025, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T13:13:31-07:00","id":1554450,"title":"","content":"As an aside: Dragon Age: Inquisitor (aka the third game) is fairly well liked in the DA fandom despite being a pretty different game from the rest too (Dragon Age doesn't really have a core identity at this point so that's a big problem); the biggest problem for Inquisitor is that skipping DAII is rough on making sense of things, and II is probably going to remain the worst game in the franchise even after Veilguard failed.<br /> <br /> I bring this up because Dragon Age was, as mentioned, mismanaged as a brand. Each game tried someone different and thus the franchise got mechanically incoherent even if Thedas as a setting got interesting as it got more and more explored and flushed out. If you like an Elder Scrolls game, the drastic odds are that you're not there for the specific mechanics that get tweaked, but the larger mechanical coherence of the game-play loop. There is a game play style to the series that's consistent from Morrowind to Skyrim, that Dragon Age never established.<br /> <br /> That is, on that side of the reviews, I think the issue at hand. There's a line between tweaking things between installments, and changing them to the point where players feel like it isn't a &quot;true&quot; sequel anymore. Players don't like buying the same exact game time after time... even if they overwhelming shell out for the same game over a radically different game when push comes to shove (see any sports video game franchise). Hitting that balance between some upgrades, some tweaks, some stuff to make the game feel fresh and worth paying again, vs. just being a glorified carbon copy of something you already have is an ever narrowing goal for video game designers working on major franchises to hit. Bethesda was really good at it for awhile (we'll see with recent high level changes in the industry if that stays true), while Bioware has a stronger reputation for being hit or miss on this.<br /> <br /> BL2 is a drastic shift of game play style from BL1, on top of things like the value of the game regardless of it's title, that's clearly not doing it favors with the early review crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T15:02:07-07:00","id":1554451,"title":"","content":"I am trying to think of THE OUTER WORLDS as one of the best AA games of all time but also remembering that it was compared against THE WITCHER and other big blockbuster RPGs. This is a game that was not a huge studio game but rescued from the darkness by people who had a love of the material. I'm not making any judgements until I play it myself but I also think that is needed. A lot of people are thinking of this as a huge game rather than a small niche one that is being made out of nostlagia for a classic title.<br /> <br /> For me, I feel a lot of people are putting AAA expectations on a AA game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T16:30:40-07:00","id":1554454,"title":"","content":"Outer Wilds was only $25 or $30 on release, so it was absolutely unfair to compare it to a $60-$70 AAA game. But with Bloodlines 2, it's charging an AAA price, so it's fair to compare it to AAA games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T17:24:02-07:00","id":1554455,"title":"","content":"My &quot;quote button&quot; isn't working right now, so it'll be by hand and a little awkward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [URL=&quot;https://forum.theonyxpath.com/&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knightingale[/URL] ]<br /> <br /> Also, when I read something like this in the <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-review/\" target=\"_blank\">PC Gamer review</a>:<br /> <br /> <i>snip</i><br /> <br /> Considering this is a full-priced game, that sounds rough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, although overall I get from the review the game is pretty good, despite problems.<br /> <br /> And in fact I do think from this review that the game may:<br /> <br /> 1 - Benefit from side-quest DLCs with better side content. If rightly priced, they may be worth it; and<br /> <br /> 2 - Deserve a sequel. Yes, I do think BL 2 is solid enough to start a franchise. Unlikely given the current stance of Paradox and their apparent fall out with TCR, but it's actually a shame it won't get one.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the already mentioned cases of franchises that ditched classic mechanics, in general they're a great way of polishing good games. In many successful franchises you have good installments that are essentially polished versions of a previous one. Heck, <i>Pokemon</i> basically live off of this, and while it's getting old it succeeded with this formula for decades.<br /> <br /> Given what they did, TCR seems reasonably capable of solving most problems, and even add the RPG mechanics absent in the game, if they're given the opportunity to continue working in BL. Not a guaranteed thing, but worth a shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [URL=&quot;https://forum.theonyxpath.com/&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy Arms[/URL] ]<br /> BL2 is a drastic shift of game play style from BL1</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true, I think a lot of the comparison really isn't fair in this particular case.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines isn't really a franchise. This is nostalgia, not continuation.<br /> <br /> Nothing really continues from one to the other from a development standpoint, it's just the IP. This is related to BL 1 in the same way <i>Sands of Time</i> is related to the original <i>Prince of Persia</i>.<br /> <br /> It's hard to say this is a franchise at all, at least for now. I don't really think comparing the two BLs is the best approach.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> [USER=&quot;12002&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">CTPhipps[/USER] ]<br /> For me, I feel a lot of people are putting AAA expectations on a AA game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some people are putting <i>Legendary</i> expectations on a new game by new people. This is a problem.<br /> <br /> But putting AAA expectations? <i><b>Paradox </b></i>put AAA expectations on the game when they charged an AAA price for it.<br /> <br /> A lot of the problem overall is that Paradox put AAA expectations on this project, they treat it as an AAA game, even when they complain is about it not living up to an AAA performance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T18:41:07-07:00","id":1554461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554455#post1554455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines isn't really a franchise. This is nostalgia, not continuation.</div> </div> </div> </div>BL2 is bad as nostalgia on multiple levels. Considering how well remakes are doing right now, if Paradox just wanted to do nostalgia, they could have released a remake of Bloodlines; esp. if the goal is to restart VtM as a video game brand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really think comparing the two BLs is the best approach. </div> </div> </div>Just as pricing makes comparing BL2 to current AAA games valid, naming makes comparing the two BLs valid. Paradox could have absolutely controlled expectations differently by not calling this game BL2, while making it clear that the game was going to be a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; to the original by being a bigger action RPG experience. Lots of games have changed IP ownership and studio developers without misunderstanding the impact of calling a new game a sequel to an older game made by other people. Paradox had access to some members of the original team and squandered that as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T21:06:03-07:00","id":1554466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554455#post1554455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My &quot;quote button&quot; isn't working right now, so it'll be by hand and a little awkward.<br /> <br /> <br /> It does, although overall I get from the review the game is pretty good, despite problems.<br /> <br /> And in fact I do think from this review that the game may:<br /> <br /> 1 - Benefit from side-quest DLCs with better side content. If rightly priced, they may be worth it; and<br /> <br /> 2 - Deserve a sequel. Yes, I do think BL 2 is solid enough to start a franchise. Unlikely given the current stance of Paradox and their apparent fall out with TCR, but it's actually a shame it won't get one.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the already mentioned cases of franchises that ditched classic mechanics, in general they're a great way of polishing good games. In many successful franchises you have good installments that are essentially polished versions of a previous one. Heck, <i>Pokemon</i> basically live off of this, and while it's getting old it succeeded with this formula for decades.<br /> <br /> Given what they did, TCR seems reasonably capable of solving most problems, and even add the RPG mechanics absent in the game, if they're given the opportunity to continue working in BL. Not a guaranteed thing, but worth a shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two DLC that have been announced sound more like story-DLC where in one you're playing another linear story through the eyes of the Brujah Sheriff in one instance and through the eyes of that Toreador lady in the other. Maybe they're giving them unique combat-powers and it sounds like Phyre gets new outfits - but that's it. There's no indication of Paradox tasking TCR to expand the game's core-mechanics or make it more of an actual RPG. <br /> <br /> The review I quoted may be overall positive and that is up to how the reviewer in question weighs various aspects of the game, but as a value-proposition the current BL2 doesn't sound that great. Like when it also mentions that it doesn't really make a difference if you play through that main-story as a Tremere or a Toreador. The differences you get through that choice are minuscule. In terms of replayability, that's not great either.<br /> <br /> And Pokemon is another bad franchise. Sure, it's still printing money. It also benefits from a bit of a monopoly because, as Palworld proves, Nintendo will come after you if you get too close to actually making a direct competitor to Pokemon. But they just released another Pokemon game on Switch 2 - and it still doesn't even have voice-acting. There's barely any innovation in those games. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554455#post1554455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is true, I think a lot of the comparison really isn't fair in this particular case.<br /> <br /> Bloodlines isn't really a franchise. This is nostalgia, not continuation.<br /> <br /> Nothing really continues from one to the other from a development standpoint, it's just the IP. This is related to BL 1 in the same way <i>Sands of Time</i> is related to the original <i>Prince of Persia</i>.<br /> <br /> It's hard to say this is a franchise at all, at least for now. I don't really think comparing the two BLs is the best approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the comparison is absolutely fair and valid, as @HeavyArms said.<br /> <br /> One, when the game was originally announced back in the day, not only did they bring on people who worked on BL1 but listen to how Paradox talked a big game back then. From an <a href=\"https://bleedingcool.com/games/paradox-interactive-announces-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/\" target=\"_blank\">article</a> about the announcement of the game in 2019:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Fans of the original Bloodlines have been hungry for a sequel for a long time, and we began to hear those suggestions \u2014 well, demands \u2014 as soon as we began to work with the World of Darkness,&quot; said Ebba Ljungerud, CEO of Paradox Interactive. &quot;We all understood what this opportunity could mean, <b>but it was essential for both us and for Hardsuit Labs that any sequel should be done properly; a true successor</b> guided by the people who knew what made the original so special. Keeping this game a secret for the last few years has been quite the Masquerade for us! It's both exciting and relieving to finally let everybody know what we have in store for them.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wonder who created the expectation that BL2 would be a true sequel...<br /> <br /> Two, there's been <a href=\"https://gameinformer.com/exclusive-interview/2025/08/15/what-makes-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-a-bloodlines-game\" target=\"_blank\">an interview with Creative Director Alex Skidrow</a> on GameInformer I mentioned in this thread before;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I ask creative director Alex Skidmore why the game is called Bloodlines 2 instead of something else, he thinks for a while, then starts his answer by saying, &quot;It's what we were asked to do.&quot; It's an honest response. Notoriously, Bloodlines 2 was originally being made by Hardsuit Labs and got far enough in development to be shown at E3 2019, but the next two years were filled with delays, departures, and ultimately, the decision to remove Hardsuit Labs from the project entirely. The Chinese Room took its place, and since it was working on a project that had already been announced, it didn't have much of a choice \u2013 this game would always be called Bloodlines 2. </div> </div> </div>Now that we have a better sense of how the game turned out, I do get the impression that the pretty linear main-story plus the Fabien-detective-stuff. That's what TCR wanted to do. The focus on combat, the side-quests and the bare-bones skill-system: That stuff only entered the picture during development once Paradox decided that the game should be called Bloodlines 2. <br /> <br /> Three, for the last year, there's been this handwringing about the released version. You got talk of a &quot;spiritual sequel&quot; and the like. But it was all this wishy-washy marketing-speak. And I think the conundrum Paradox faced here is that once the first trailers for the TCR version started appearing, you got a lot of criticisms along the lines of &quot;This isn't a true sequel, is it?&quot;. The problem after that was... that the critics were right. This wouldn't be a true sequel. And more, if it isn't a true sequel, why call it Bloodlines 2 to begin with? And the problem Paradox faced on that front is that the honest answer to that question is that there isn't a good answer. Because I think ultimately the real reason this thing was released as Bloodlines 2 is because Paradox just wanted to finally put something out called &quot;Bloodlines 2&quot;. Of course, the pressure to actually finally release something despite all the drama/development-hell-stuff was just yet another self-inflicted wound created by Paradox. But considering how they talked last year, I get the sense they were at the point where they had simply given up and they just wanted something, <i>anything </i>really, to be put out there that would allow them to say &quot;We released Bloodlines 2.&quot;. Of course, it's not nice for TCR that Paradox pushed them to release the game with that sort of mindset but well, here we are...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T00:53:54-07:00","id":1554468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554461#post1554461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BL2 is bad as nostalgia on multiple levels. Considering how well remakes are doing right now, if Paradox just wanted to do nostalgia, they could have released a remake of Bloodlines; esp. if the goal is to restart VtM as a video game brand.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably would have been better, that's for certain.<br /> <br /> Overall I think Paradox made a lot of mistakes. But precisely because of those, this game being as good as it apparently is is almost a miracle.<br /> <br /> But you're right. Naming the game differently or making a remake would both be valid and better decisions. Not decisions Paradox would make, but that's on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554466#post1554466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no indication of Paradox tasking TCR to expand the game's core-mechanics or make it more of an actual RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Paradox will do it, just that it would be good.<br /> <br /> They already practically said they plan on just giving it minimal attention for as long as they're absolutely required and then ditch the whole thing for the next project.<br /> <br /> Also it doesn't seem like either of them want to work with the other again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554466#post1554466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of replayability, that's not great either.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the same time, the fact that the responses you get depend on how you played indicates another gameplay element that does reward replayability.<br /> <br /> My point isn't that the game is awesome, but it is good. It's apparently far better than my expectations.<br /> <br /> I personally still think that comparing it to BL 1 is beating a dead horse. The AAA pricing is obviously bad. Both those points are well established to me.<br /> <br /> But it <i><b>seems</b></i> to be a good game <i>on its own terms</i>. And if not one that's worth USD 60, still one that's worth buying at some point in a sale, a game that will be fun to play.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554466#post1554466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Pokemon is another bad franchise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but it is the most didactic I could think about to showcase my point.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554466#post1554466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ultimately the real reason this thing was released as Bloodlines 2 is because Paradox just wanted to finally put something out called &quot;Bloodlines 2</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe my problem is that this is kind of old news to me.<br /> <br /> The whole project started like that. Paradox literally said they were looking for someone to make BL 2, then they got Hardsuit Labs. It's hard to say how much HL wanted to make BL 2 or just had to name whatever they did BL 2, Paradox itself never had an actual plan for the game, just the goal of releasing Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> When you add to that their history, and how their mistakes and strategies are regular and predictable, you know they wouldn't change this goal for nothing short of complete despair. Because that's a point of pride for them that they'll see any project to its completion, even way past the point where it's worth it, unless it really becomes impossible to make. They're stupidly stubborn, although they like to think they're honorable or something, but really that means this thing would be BL 2 because nothing would dissuade Paradox from naming this thing BL 2.<br /> <br /> I didn't really expected the name to mean much by them. What we're seeing right now is well within my expectations of how faithful it would be to the original. In fact I thought it could be worse, not necessarily would, but could. And it would be called BL 2 nonetheless because Paradox would be Paradox.<br /> <br /> But as far as it as a continuation goes, I do agree that it's bad. It's just that it's less bad than I thought it would be, and on top of that seems to be an ok game, far better than I expected after development hell. Which is another thing for me: after everything that happened, it was running the risk of being a proper continuation, but a horrible game, which would be even worse.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T01:41:00-07:00","id":1554471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554468#post1554468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole project started like that. Paradox literally said they were looking for someone to make BL 2, then they got Hardsuit Labs. It's hard to say how much HL wanted to make BL 2 or just had to name whatever they did BL 2, Paradox itself never had an actual plan for the game, just the goal of releasing Bloodlines 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think Paradox and HSL did want to make an actual Bloodlines 2. That was the goal of bringing Mitsoda and a few other members of the original Bloodlines 1 team onto the project, to give Bloodlines 2 authenticity. <br /> <br /> &quot;See, we didn't just make a vampire game and slap the name Bloodlines on it, it's an actual sequel to the original game written by one of the original game's primary writers.&quot; That was kind of a big part of the initial marketing Paradox was using to build hype.<br /> <br /> I do agree after HSL shut down it seems like Paradox just wanted to get a game called Bloodlines 2 out so they had Chinese room make a game and slapped the name on it. And from interviews, I never got the feeling Chinese Room wanted to specifically make <i>Bloodlines 2</i> but were more interested in making a vampire game in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T03:49:05-07:00","id":1554472,"title":"","content":"Actually, from what I understand it is the reverse for HSL and TCR.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case may be, Hardsuit Labs is the beastie that decided that Brian Mitsoda and Chris Avellone would be terminated from the project and all of their work on the side projects removed. This despite the fact both men were intregal to getting Bloodlines up and running in the first place. Chris Avellone's accusations (retracted or not) gave a reason for the latter but Brian Mitsoda was just removed for no reason other than it seems no one wanted him for anything other than marketing. Indeed, Brian has alluded to the fact they wanted him to do way more interviews than writing (and he hated that).<br /> <br /> We may never know the whole story but the implications have always been that Hardsuit Labs was nowhere near close to finishing the game, likes years away and dropping those writers didn't help (but the fact they didn't have their material adapted shows how far behind they were). So Paradox shut it down like Gordon Ramsey in Hell's Kitchen. The project was dead.<br /> <br /> However, the Chinese Room approached Paradox (not the other way around) and had their own passionate vision for the game. They didn't just want to &quot;finish&quot; the game despite having all of the previous assets. They wanted to do their own story with an Elder. That shows they are more than just someone churning out slop for a paycheck. This is a project they believe in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T08:14:42-07:00","id":1554476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554472#post1554472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the Chinese Room approached Paradox (not the other way around) and had their own passionate vision for the game. They didn't just want to &quot;finish&quot; the game despite having all of the previous assets. They wanted to do their own story with an Elder. That shows they are more than just someone churning out slop for a paycheck. This is a project they believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression was that Chinese Room approached Paradox because they wanted to do a Vampire game. Paradox said sure. Chinese Room started working on their game and then they were informed that the Vampire game they were going to release was going to be Bloodlines 2. Chinese Room didn't specifically set out to make Bloodlines 2, they only found out that their game was going to be Bloodlines 2 a bit later.<br /> <br /> But we'll probably never know the actual details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T11:10:44-07:00","id":1554479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554471#post1554471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do think Paradox and HSL did want to make an actual Bloodlines 2. That was the goal of bringing Mitsoda and a few other members of the original Bloodlines 1 team onto the project, to give Bloodlines 2 authenticity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but I won't say for certain because we don't have many key details.<br /> <br /> From the very beginning this was a project Paradox was willing to interfere with to some degree, but not really participate. It's likely that Paradox, not HL, was the sole responsible for bringing original BL crew. That means this says nothing about what HL really wanted to do, and their later actions seem to indicate they didn't really want this interference.<br /> <br /> But more on point, I said Paradox never had a plan for the game, and they didn't. They had a vague goal of having something the public recognized as a proper sequel, but that alone isn't a plan, they made it very clear that they didn't participate in the development at all. So all that remains is the actual intentions of Hardsuit Labs, and those we won't know for the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the first full year of delays was itself a strong indication that whatever they would do, was going to be bad. And when TCR entered the picture it was plenty clear that the game would be whatever VTM slapped with the BL 2 name, especially since Paradox outright said they were given freedom to start from scratch. And actually that's also the reason the game got a chance of at least being good in the first place, but the chances of it being an actual sequel were close to zero by then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554472#post1554472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, from what I understand it is the reverse for HSL and TCR.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point isn't how much each wanted to make a vampire game, but how much they wanted to do an actual sequel.<br /> <br /> For all the problems HL's development had, we have no reason to think they didn't planned an actual sequel, i.e. a game with similar-but-updated mechanics and related story. I think we have reason to not take this for granted, but that's as far as we can get. Thinking you have a better idea for an author's story than the author themselves <b>is a thing</b>, so who know why they didn't want Mitsoda &amp; Co..<br /> <br /> Chinese Room wanted to make a game. And they did make a game. That's clear as day. But it seems they never wanted their game <i><u>to be Bloodlines 2</u></i>. That's all.<br /> <br /> No one here's saying any of the two just wanted to churn out slop for a paycheck. In fact, that's clearly not the case, since slop is easy and fast to make. We don't know why HL failed and delayed, maybe we'll never know, and it may be for a number of reasons, from incompetence to unforeseeable problems to bad faith. But if they were just making slop, we would have gotten the game in time and it would be terrible. Although it's possible they tried and were caught by Paradox, who knows?<br /> <br /> We can't really say what HL was doing or planning. We can't really say if they believed in the project at some point, I don't think this is a helpful analysis. We can say, though, that Paradox initially wanted the game to be recognized by the public. And we can say that TCR didn't want a proper sequel (and they didn't made one). Yet we also can say for sure that TCR did have a game in mind and worked well on it.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T14:07:37-07:00","id":1554494,"title":"","content":"I think it's Bloodlines 2 if it's about exploring a new city in Vampire: The Masquerade but that's because I think the primary purpose of the Bloodlines game is a single player V:TM experience.<br /> <br /> But we'll find out in two days if the game is what people want or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T19:49:26-07:00","id":1554504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554494#post1554494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's Bloodlines 2 if it's about exploring a new city in Vampire: The Masquerade but that's because I think the primary purpose of the Bloodlines game is a single player V:TM experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm whiling to give a pass to BL 2 because of its development history, but besides that...<br /> <br /> No, this is too vague. At the very least we should see similar mechanics. <i>Bloodlines</i> wasn't just single player VTM in a city, it was a translation of the Tabletop system and how in it customization opens completely new avenues for problem solving. Being able to change a lot of how your character work (and not just powers) through character creation was fundamental to the experience, and so was the possibility of navigating most challenges with at least three unrelated approaches (usually Combat vs Stealth vs Social).<br /> <br /> Single player VTM experience exploring a city is kind of what I would expect to be standard fare for an AA VTM game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T00:05:14-07:00","id":1554512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554504#post1554504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm whiling to give a pass to BL 2 because of its development history, but besides that...<br /> <br /> No, this is too vague. At the very least we should see similar mechanics. <i>Bloodlines</i> wasn't just single player VTM in a city, it was a translation of the Tabletop system and how in it customization opens completely new avenues for problem solving. Being able to change a lot of how your character work (and not just powers) through character creation was fundamental to the experience, and so was the possibility of navigating most challenges with at least three unrelated approaches (usually Combat vs Stealth vs Social).<br /> <br /> Single player VTM experience exploring a city is kind of what I would expect to be standard fare for an AA VTM game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the VTM system translated incredibly poorly to video games and often cut off content. If they wanted to do a Bloodlines adaptation, I would have made changing the stats to be the top priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-20T20:40:28-07:00","id":1554534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554512#post1554512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the VTM system translated incredibly poorly to video games and often cut off content. If they wanted to do a Bloodlines adaptation, I would have made changing the stats to be the top priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and?<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines</i> did it, and this greatly defined the game. And I didn't said it had to be VTM native system <i>as is</i>, that's irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Making a huge map with a shitton of vehicles and then have every single one of them work according to type and model, with a mechanic for hijacking, despite that literally not being the actual point of the game (despite title), is hard, yet it is the defining mechanic of GTA. I won't say any open world action game about a criminal exploring a city is GTA.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not terribly pissed off by BL 2's name <i>in specific</i>, but BL certainly has something to distinguish it beyond &quot;VTM in a 