of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-21T11:17:38-07:00","id":1554546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554544#post1554544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, this game plays much more like Dishonored/Deux Ex: Human Revolution than Bloodlines, I admit it. That isn't a bad thing, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Can you explain?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-21T12:57:27-07:00","id":1554550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554546#post1554546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so? Can you explain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The game basically is a mixture of stealth and hand to hand combat. There's a lot of combat that is unavoidable, which is a shame and you'll have to have a bunch of fights throughout the game. There's also the fact quite a few places are arenas where you have to sneak past people or kill them or both. However, there's not nearly as much focus on stealth as I thought nor assassination but primarily hand to hand and using your disciplines for crowd control.<br /> <br /> The best parts of the game are the conversation, atmosphere, and manipulating other Kindred. There's a lot of questions and responses that will screw you up so you have to pick wisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T14:54:43-07:00","id":1554565,"title":"","content":"A little correction: I just confirmed that Mitsoda was indeed hired directly by HL even before they pitched to Paradox, and they did reveal some of their goals to the game at the time, that included changes to core mechanics, but not ditching them the way TCR did.<br /> <br /> So I think they both had an actual vision for the game and it was, by then, an actual sequel.<br /> <br /> The reasons behind Mitsoda's termination are still a mystery, as are most of the development problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T16:21:54-07:00","id":1554568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554550#post1554550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game basically is a mixture of stealth and hand to hand combat. There's a lot of combat that is unavoidable, which is a shame and you'll have to have a bunch of fights throughout the game. There's also the fact quite a few places are arenas where you have to sneak past people or kill them or both. However, there's not nearly as much focus on stealth as I thought nor assassination but primarily hand to hand and using your disciplines for crowd control.<br /> <br /> The best parts of the game are the conversation, atmosphere, and manipulating other Kindred. There's a lot of questions and responses that will screw you up so you have to pick wisely.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a game that's based on a property with magic concealment powers (<a href=\"https://www.ccgtrader.net/card/34998/you-cant-see-me-im-a-vampire\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;You Can't See Me, I'm a Vampire!&quot;</a>), the fact that it seems to emphasize stealth only about as much as Wolfenstein: the New Colossus is... weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T16:26:13-07:00","id":1554570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554568#post1554568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a game that's based on a property with magic concealment powers (<a href=\"https://www.ccgtrader.net/card/34998/you-cant-see-me-im-a-vampire\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;You Can't See Me, I'm a Vampire!&quot;</a>), the fact that it seems to emphasize stealth only about as much as Wolfenstein: the New Colossus is... weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it's much more Batman than Wolfenstein as you can't do anything really save in alleyways or on rooftops. The game's Masquerade is pretty generous but the game has you doing all your Kung Fu vampire fights in the skyline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554565#post1554565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little correction: I just confirmed that Mitsoda was indeed hired directly by HL even before they pitched to Paradox, and they did reveal some of their goals to the game at the time, that included changes to core mechanics, but not ditching them the way TCR did.<br /> <br /> So I think they both had an actual vision for the game and it was, by then, an actual sequel.<br /> <br /> The reasons behind Mitsoda's termination are still a mystery, as are most of the development problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris Avellone's article on it basically suggests he and Mitsoda were constantly championing Bloodlines 2 and for lack of any other source, I'd say it was trustworthy.<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://chrisavellone.medium.com/what-the-fuck-happened-to-bloodlines-2-1ad557bf2284\" target=\"_blank\">A reminder here</a>)<br /> <br /> However, with the other information, I think they were cutting a lot of people off because they were nowhere near release and way over budget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-22-2025, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T17:15:03-07:00","id":1554573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554570#post1554570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue it's much more Batman than Wolfenstein as you can't do anything really save in alleyways or on rooftops.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's even weirder. By the time the late-game <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">fake-out execution and grafting his head onto an ubersoldat body</div></div> </div> </div> hits and BJ is fully in his stride, he can somehow out-slither Setites to access out of the way places and alternate routes. Which would also be theoretically bypassed with elder mist forms or earth-creepin'.<br /> <br /> Also, how Batman it is really depends on how often the elder uses guns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game's Masquerade is pretty generous but the game has you doing all your Kung Fu vampire fights in the skyline. </div> </div> </div>I suspect that people would probably enjoy it a lot less if it got every Kindred and SI op in the city on you just for using your neat cool powers. Also, that would probably take a fair bit of processor power to make work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T05:51:14-07:00","id":1554591,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this shit is getting 3/10 from me.<br /> Combat is janky, characters are bad, their face animations are non-existent, Masquerade system is a joke (even Battle Royale Bloodhunt has a better system), side quest are nothing burger, 3 day old Prince and her shitty court barely functions and way too arrogant to survive. In fact I wonder how they survived since they make LaCroix look competent. They don't even know how to behave towards an Elder, nevermind that they can't even keep the Masquerade intact since you have the local Seattle newspaper talking about superhuman criminals with witness testimony.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not even Combat makes you feel like a powerful Elder when all you fight are Ghouls, &quot;Elite&quot; Thinbloods and Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T08:37:29-07:00","id":1554595,"title":"","content":"LaCroix <u><b>was</b></u> competent. Not terribly so, but he was.<br /> <br /> His biggest problem was actually that he was in a shitty position, the result of either too much ambition or a set-up against him.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla didn't really control LA. Even if some vampires in the city were allied to the Cam, they didn't really control much to begin with, or care all that much. Some of the vampires in the city were older and more powerful than LaCroix, they just didn't want the position for one reason or another. And the game happens during a tipping point where everything that could go wrong is going wrong simultaneously.<br /> <br /> Overall he's good in his role in <i>Bloodlines</i> precisely because he's a serious enough threat, even if not a overwhelming one (far from it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T01:23:30-07:00","id":1554761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554544#post1554544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I HAVE MY COPY!<br /> <br /> So far, I'm quite impressed.<br /> <br /> And yes, this game plays much more like Dishonored/Deux Ex: Human Revolution than Bloodlines, I admit it. That isn't a bad thing, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This description confuses me because Bloodlines 1 already plays like Deus Ex. It's an ImSim. You have a hub world from which you go into mission instances. You can blast through the level or go scurry in the vents or do a mysterious third thing. In the hub world you can chat with NPCs and pick up some side quests to do in that hub world, and find/buy extra gear that'll help you on missions.<br /> <br /> If anything, the problem with Bloodlines 2 is that it <i>doesn't</i> play like an Immerisive Sim despite looking like one. It has a hub world but the hub world is empty. It has vents, but the vents are part of the linear movement road rather than an option. It's like a simulacrum of an ImSim. It knows that there are certain features that ImSims have, so it also has them, but it doesn't know why or what to do with them to make the game fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T01:52:33-07:00","id":1554763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554761#post1554761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This description confuses me because Bloodlines 1 already plays like Deus Ex. It's an ImSim. You have a hub world from which you go into mission instances. You can blast through the level or go scurry in the vents or do a mysterious third thing. In the hub world you can chat with NPCs and pick up some side quests to do in that hub world, and find/buy extra gear that'll help you on missions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am wondering if we're talking past one another because you're describing Bloodlines 2 (with alchemy replacing gear).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T05:48:01-07:00","id":1554766,"title":"","content":"So, now I've finished my playthrough and overall... I would call it a mediocre action-adventure with a decent story. But really, pretty much every facet of the game is a mixed bag. The story is still the strongest part - even though it's quite linear, sometimes to the point of feeling like you're getting railroaded. That's still the part I liked the most, though.<br /> <br /> There are two obvious issues this game deals with: First, its name and second, its price.<br /> <br /> Is it a worthy sequel to Bloodlines 1? No, absolutely not. And I don't think calling it an RPG fits here. Like I mentioned, it feels more like an action-adventure type of game to me. I'd compare more to something like the Crystal Dynamics Tomb Raider reboot games. You have combat-scenes, a very basic skill-system and a pretty linear story (with some side-quests). But character-progression, skill-systems, inventory, story-choices... All of that is either completely missing or present in such a basic manner that RPG doesn't fit as a description of this game.<br /> <br /> But the second issue is the price. Does this game feel like a full-price game? Not really. If anything, just looking at the game, I'd feel more comfortable thinking of it as a solid AA-type of game. There's important stuff missing, like a FOV-slider, the option to turn off motion-blur and accessibility-options regarding color and the like. Hopefully, they will patch that into the game in the near future. But releasing a full-prices game without those options is bad. There's also the feeling that a lot of what this game has to offer in terms of gameplay feels shoddy or unpolished if you're expecting something on the level of a full-priced game. <br /> <br /> Combat and the Disciplines are... okay. I wish they had mapped light and heavy attack to two different buttons. You don't have a block which is weird but you do have a dodge. And later I figured out that you can counter attacks by dashing into enemies but it all felt weird. The telekinesis was useless in combat unless you activated vampire vision. And vampire vision is that typical detective mode feature from way back when Batman Arkham Asylum came out. It has a similar issue where you use this special vision to gain more information but at the same time you're also looking at an uglier version of the game-world. Here, in Bloodlines 2, you kinda have to use vampire vision to see the objects you can pick up via telekinesis. Later on, that got a little bit easier. Other than that, the flow of combat when people are getting thrown around due to your heavy attacks and the animation of feeding in combat (as well as the finishing animations) looks good and you feel strong in those moments. So that works. But it also gets repetitive quickly due to a lack of variety in the animations. <br /> <br /> For my playthrough, I picked Ventrue and... it did say easy. I played around with the other powers a little bit to compare as well. But the game wasn't kidding when it called Ventrue the easy option. By far, the best set of powers and the two Passives are very useful as well (temporary damage reduction after feeding and feeding heals more). If I were to play it again, I think I would pick Lasombra because that power-set felt the most interesting in my opinion. Tremere was also interesting, though. But the passives for Tremere aren't that good.<br /> <br /> The gameworld looks nice but the Resonance-stuff, the sidequests, the Masquerade-meter... Really, all of it is so rudimentary and boring that it just worsened my opinion of the game. The end-effect: Later on, I just dashed through the city to get to the next quest-marker. I had lost any interest in the game-world outside of the main-story-missions. <br /> <br /> So, overall, as an AA action adventure game, it feels okay. But I think on one hand, it's a miracle that this game came out at all after all the development-hell drama and there's nothing disastrously wrong with this game. On the other hand, though, there isn't a single aspect in this game that stands out positively either. <br /> <br /> So, for me, it's a 5/10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T10:03:47-07:00","id":1554778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/bloodlines-2-halloween-update\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/u73tyf0fa8v1/4GtNkTwc3KD5wcl5iZfw6H/412090a992d51ec9d468cacc1ccfab7a/bloodlines2-web-header.webp?w=1200&amp;h=630&amp;fit=fill&amp;f=center\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/bloodlines-2-halloween-update\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 - Halloween Update - Paradox Interactive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/bloodlines-2-halloween-update\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/bloodlines-2-halloween-update </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 - You are the Nomad. An elder vampire awakening from a century-long slumber, new to the modern nights. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;In future updates, we\u2019re looking at including features such as an FOV slider, new save game options, custom difficulty settings that include the ability to play only Phyre\u2019s side of the story on your second playthrough, as well as additional customization options.&quot;<br /> <br /> The turnaround with Bloodlines 2 acting on the feedback of fans is amazing. Now I'm hoping we can get some extra sidequests. That will obviously take more time, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T10:14:07-07:00","id":1554779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554778#post1554778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/bloodlines-2-halloween-update\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/g...lloween-update</a><br /> <br /> &quot;In future updates, we\u2019re looking at including features such as an FOV slider, new save game options, custom difficulty settings that include the ability to play only Phyre\u2019s side of the story on your second playthrough, as well as additional customization options.&quot;<br /> <br /> The turnaround with Bloodlines 2 acting on the feedback of fans is amazing. Now I'm hoping we can get some extra sidequests. That will obviously take more time, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the words I would use to describe this are &quot;incompetent&quot; and &quot;unacceptable&quot;. When it comes to full-price games, <i>these options need to be there on day 1</i>. Period. Anything less than that is unacceptable. That's why complaining about it is important and companies need to be pushed again and again to get away from the intolerant practice of treating accessibility-options like an afterthought. And Paradox/Chinese Room did engage in intolerant behavior here by not having basic, let me emphasize here, BASIC accessibility-options in their full-priced game on day 1. <br /> <br /> And the save-game-options... Still can't figure out why they didn't have manual saves in the game. Such a basic thing. Again, that's why one word that perfectly describes Bloodlines 2 right now is &quot;unpolished&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T10:49:02-07:00","id":1554780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554779#post1554779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the words I would use to describe this are &quot;incompetent&quot; and &quot;unacceptable&quot;. When it comes to full-price games, <i>these options need to be there on day 1</i>. Period. Anything less than that is unacceptable. That's why complaining about it is important and companies need to be pushed again and again to get away from the intolerant practice of treating accessibility-options like an afterthought. And Paradox/Chinese Room did engage in intolerant behavior here by not having basic, let me emphasize here, BASIC accessibility-options in their full-priced game on day 1.<br /> <br /> And the save-game-options... Still can't figure out why they didn't have manual saves in the game. Such a basic thing. Again, that's why one word that perfectly describes Bloodlines 2 right now is &quot;unpolished&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a hilarious post on another forum where under the above I added, &quot;I bet there's going to be a lot of fans who go, 'this should have been day one' rather than realizing a major developer doing a turnaround from fan feedback in a week is fantastic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just glad they're going to continue supporting the game through 2026. It makes me hope there will be an option to clean up Phyre's apartment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T11:11:24-07:00","id":1554781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554780#post1554780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a hilarious post on another forum where under the above I added, &quot;I bet there's going to be a lot of fans who go, 'this should have been day one' rather than realizing a major developer doing a turnaround from fan feedback in a week is fantastic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just glad they're going to continue supporting the game through 2026. It makes me hope there will be an option to clean up Phyre's apartment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because it is scandalous that it isn't a day on feature. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bIt wouldn't be &quot; fantastic&quot; if a major company like McDonald were to open restaurants with no toilets, and when people rightfully complain, then they decide to put some. <br /> <br /> So of course people are complaining about it. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T11:41:52-07:00","id":1554783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554780#post1554780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a hilarious post on another forum where under the above I added, &quot;I bet there's going to be a lot of fans who go, 'this should have been day one' rather than realizing a major developer doing a turnaround from fan feedback in a week is fantastic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm just glad they're going to continue supporting the game through 2026. It makes me hope there will be an option to clean up Phyre's apartment.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the accessibility-option-issue is a general videogame-industry-issue. I remember back in the day when people like Totalbiscuit were complaining about the lack of FOV-sliders. That was more than 10 years ago. I think with most AAA-releases, it is now standard to have these options and that is good. But that's why I say this feels like an AA-game. It's a sign of a bad full-priced game to not have put this into the game on day 1. <br /> <br /> And &quot;realizing a major developer doing a turnaround from fan feedback in a week is fantastic&quot; is utter nonsense. There are people who, for example, get sick when motion blur occurs and not addressing that on day 1 is terrible. Imagine the person who pre-ordered the game and who gets sick because of motion-blur, then plays the game on day 1 and realizes they can't because of the motion-blur? Apparently, you would just tell that person: &quot;Sucks to be you. I don't care. Maybe they will fix that later.&quot;. And what I'm saying is that if you're buying a full-price videogame in 2025, you're entitled to having the option to turn off motion-blur, for example. Therefore, if, as a reviewer, I notice it being absent, I'm gonna call this out as an obviously bad thing.<br /> <br /> Everything outlined in that update you've linked to should've been there on day 1. I don't know why you're showing this much tolerance for obvious negligence and bad design. This is like saying the state of Cyberpunk 2077 at launch was fine because it's now a better game. You need to have better standards. This is another general videogames-issue: The state of the game on day 1 matters. If it's shit on day 1 and gets better later on, that still means the publisher/developer was willing to release/sell a game in a state that's shit. And that's unacceptable. <br /> <br /> And again, it's because people like me and many others are complaining about features like a lack of a FOV-sliders that this update will happen. But you gotta understand: This is them responding to <i>issues </i>people have. So, while, yes, it's good that they address them but it's also relevant to point out <i>that they created these problems in the first place</i>. This isn't them fulfilling wishes from fans; this is them trying to fix problems with the game. Putting the FOV-slider in like this post-launch is them admitting that they've fucked up. So, rather than calling it &quot;amazing&quot;, I'd call it &quot;the bare minimum of addressing their fuck-up&quot;. <br /> <br /> What is now happening is a process of the developer trying to fix a bunch of their mistakes. There's nothing &quot;amazing&quot; about the fact that Bloodlines 2 will have to address a big list of issues with this game if it wants to get a better reception from the players. And there's nothing admirable about doing this post-launch for a full-priced game. If the development-process had been effective, there would've been no need for this but clearly mistakes have happened here. Who knows why they've happened but there are clearly a bunch of issues TCR now will have to fix in the upcoming weeks. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T12:55:19-07:00","id":1554787,"title":"","content":"The changelog of fixes they did make is also staggeringly bad from the perspective of (1) day 1 experience with the game and (2) destroying trust in quality control for the product.<br /> <br /> The sheer number of game breaking (&quot;title crash&quot;) bugs in a AAA priced game? Awful. A giant list of soft locks that needed fixing (and worse in a game with no manual saves, so that means a complete restart)? Abysmal.<br /> <br /> That's a list of bugs that would tank most &quot;A&quot; or &quot;AA&quot; studios if it happened to their biggest game launch.<br /> <br /> There's still massive UE5 optimization problems with the game. This is a single player game that can't maintain a constant 60 fps even with a top of the line gaming PC.<br /> <br /> It's also not a great look to release a bunch of cosmetics for, again, a single player game when such serious fundamental problems were present and launch and there's a laundry list of unfixed problems. You don't have time to add some spooky looks for your horror-adjacent title if the game is literally unplayable for some people, because those people aren't going to want to come back to see if the problem is fixed when you make it clear your priorities are fancy skins instead of game-essentials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T13:32:44-07:00","id":1554791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554787#post1554787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changelog of fixes they did make is also staggeringly bad from the perspective of (1) day 1 experience with the game and (2) destroying trust in quality control for the product.<br /> <br /> The sheer number of game breaking (&quot;title crash&quot;) bugs in a AAA priced game? Awful. A giant list of soft locks that needed fixing (and worse in a game with no manual saves, so that means a complete restart)? Abysmal.<br /> <br /> That's a list of bugs that would tank most &quot;A&quot; or &quot;AA&quot; studios if it happened to their biggest game launch.<br /> <br /> There's still massive UE5 optimization problems with the game. This is a single player game that can't maintain a constant 60 fps even with a top of the line gaming PC.<br /> <br /> <b>It's also not a great look to release a bunch of cosmetics for, again, a single player game when such serious fundamental problems were present and launch and there's a laundry list of unfixed problems.</b> You don't have time to add some spooky looks for your horror-adjacent title if the game is literally unplayable for some people, because those people aren't going to want to come back to see if the problem is fixed when you make it clear your priorities are fancy skins instead of game-essentials.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Turns to stare at Koei-Tecmo as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T13:36:32-07:00","id":1554792,"title":"","content":"Let's face it, the only reason we can't turn to stare at even more companies is so much of the industry is focused on games with multiplayer experiences where mtx for skins/etc. can rake in the big cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T14:37:28-07:00","id":1554794,"title":"","content":"After playing for a second as a different clan:<br /> <br /> Re-playability is pretty minor and honestly not worth it. Especially the Fabien sections.<br /> I am going to revise my score to 4/10, if only because I stopped thinking it as a Bloodlines game.<br /> <br /> If they branded this as anything but Bloodlines, halved the price and polished some stuff, this could have been solid 7/10 game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27335,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","user":"Technoma","date":". 10-29-2025, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T15:29:49-07:00","id":1554797,"title":"","content":"I agree that the fixes regarding able gameplay are Day 1 needed.<br /> <br /> But I'm confused at anyone referring to this as an AAA game. Isn't it and hasn't it always been a AA game? What made people think this was a AAA game? This has always been something done by a 30 person studio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T16:01:36-07:00","id":1554799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554797#post1554797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the fixes regarding able gameplay are Day 1 needed.<br /> <br /> But I'm confused at anyone referring to this as an AAA game. Isn't it and hasn't it always been a AA game? What made people think this was a AAA game? This has always been something done by a 30 person studio.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It's AAA because anything with a 60+$ price-tag is considered AAA. We're slowly getting to the point where 70 bucks becomes the new standard but it used to be 60. The reason you simply act as if it's AAA is because those are the type of games you'd be competing with. Outer Worlds 2 (Obsidian/Microsoft), Battlefield 6 (EA), Anno 117: Pax Romana (Ubisoft)... Now those are genuine AAA-developers/publishers obviously, but this is the competition when your game costs 60+$. And so, yeah, I think it's completely acceptable to hold Bloodlines 2 to the same standard as you would Outer Worlds 2.</li> <li>The <a href=\"https://www.gamesindustry.biz/the-chinese-room-is-independent-again-heres-how-it-happened\" target=\"_blank\">most recent reporting</a> (when the Chinese Room went independent) said that it's a studio employing 55 developers.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T19:25:20-07:00","id":1554807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554778#post1554778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;In future updates, we\u2019re looking at including features such as an FOV slider, new save game options, custom difficulty settings that include the ability to play only Phyre\u2019s side of the story on your second playthrough, as well as additional customization options.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say their response to fans is &quot;amazing&quot;, but it is good.<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> said, what they launched is quite weak for the price tag. Mistakes that could be easily forgiven in an AA-priced game, but this is not an AA-priced game. For what they're asking, it was incompetent work, and answering to complaints is the least they should do.<br /> <br /> That said, praise where praise is due, their response has been above expectation. Not terribly, but surprising nonetheless. And it is possible that this attitude will save this game in the long run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554780#post1554780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a hilarious post on another forum</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not hilarious, it's disrespectful.<br /> <br /> Those people are right, because those are things that should be expected in an AAA game.<br /> <br /> You willfully ignore that this is a game with a full price and a strong (however problematic) marketing machine behind it. You oversell the positives and undersell the negatives, hugely.<br /> <br /> And most important, you refuse to recognize that those complaints are common because they're meaningful to people. You don't engage them, you jump to the positives again and again without addressing what people said.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554797#post1554797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm confused at anyone referring to this as an AAA game. Isn't it and hasn't it always been a AA game? What made people think this was a AAA game? This has always been something done by a 30 person studio.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the producer matters. This is a Paradox game, this is not a TCR game all by itself and with only their own resources.<br /> <br /> Second, it costs as an AAA. If you ask an AAA price, you get an AAA scrutiny. Period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T19:57:51-07:00","id":1554812,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AAA_(video_game_industry\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AAA_(video_game_industry</a>)<br /> <br /> Well, according to Wikipedia, a AAA game is defined not by how much is charged for the game but by the development and marketing budgets for the game.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not trying to get into an argument, though as my own opinions on the subject are that the game was extremely flawed and I massively lowered my usual positivity for these sorts of projects. I wanted to give a much more balanced perspective on the subject. I feel like I've done that by pointing out what I determined to be the flaws of the games in my review. If you disagree, though, that's your opinion and I'm comparing the game perhaps unfairly to CDPR.<br /> <br /> The game that released from CDPR (Cyberpunk 2077) is one of my all time favorite of all time but was released in a broken unfinished state and it took years to get it into a proper form. Worse, they didn't respond immediately to the outrage over the many issues within it. So yes, I am very happy they're (The Chinese Room) addressing mistakes within a reasonable time limit.<br /> <br /> I don't begrudge people that think that's still too late.<br /> <br /> It's my hope they continue to add to the game, repair its mistakes, and make it a better experience that modders can continue to expand on until it becomes the same sort of cult classic that Bloodlines 1 was.<br /> <br /> I won't comment further on that element and appreciate everyone taking the time to discuss the issue with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-29-2025, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T20:19:53-07:00","id":1554815,"title":"","content":"And I apologize for being dismissive. That was unfair and I know everyone is just voicing their valid concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T14:17:15-08:00","id":1554983,"title":"","content":"The problem is that shoddy releases like this one are directly connected to releases like Mind's Eye from this year. This whole idea of &quot;Fixing it post-launch is okay.&quot; is just telling greedy assholes that it's okay to release games in the state Cyberpunk 2077 was in on day 1 or the aforementioned Mind's Eye from this year. <br /> <br /> And what's really bizarre is how games-development have gotten worse because of digital sales. Used to be, when you announced a release-date, you had to account for getting the game finished, then getting it printed on discs and then getting those in stores. That was a lengthy process. With digital sales, you don't need to do any of that anymore. Yeah, more time for developers to work on the game! Or so you might think... What happened instead is that crunch happens until the last minute before the game goes public - and it all comes down to the &quot;Day 1 Patch&quot;. Except increasingly... it's not about the &quot;Day 1 Patch&quot; anymore. Now it's about the Day 30 Patch or something like that because the public release seems to happen somewhere close to the end of development. Rather, you're actually just paying them to be a beta-tester. <br /> <br /> And the worst part is: None of this should be needed in the first place. I mean, come on... you seriously need people playing the game and complaining about it to figure out that a first-person-game (costing 60+$) without a FOV-slider in 2025 is an issue? Nah, the real issue is the publisher. I mean, look at the game. All of it, I mean. All these supposed &quot;features&quot;. And now let's remember that according to Paradox, this game should've come out last year in October. This game looks shoddy and unpolished in a lot of areas but somehow Paradox was confident that the release-date would be October 2024. In hindsight, it just seems insane how Paradox have fumbled this. Honestly, if anything, I would've wanted TCR to spend more time developing this game because of how undercooked parts of it feel. And yet, the TCR-version of the game had already gotten two delays. <br /> <br /> Hopefully, the moment of Paradox throwing TCR under the bus won't be too harsh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T14:26:03-08:00","id":1554985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554983#post1554983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully, the moment of Paradox throwing TCR under the bus won't be too harsh...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, they've promised continued patching and fixing through 2026 so they won't be doing that. I'd rather a game that is made better than abandonware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-02T14:43:53-08:00","id":1554987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553270-bloodlines-2-release-day-and-content?p=1554985#post1554985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thankfully, they've promised continued patching and fixing through 2026 so they won't be doing that. I'd rather a game that is made better than abandonware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the issue is that they can't both patch the game <i>and </i>work on the DLC at the same time. Unless... the two bits of DLC are super-short, of course. Then again, story-on-rails doing the same-old shticks from the main-game... Maybe it won't be that difficult to do it. You just gotta get those voice-actors back in a booth. And voila, you have two story-DLCs.<br /> <br /> And I don't think you should have any confidence in Paradox-leadership when it comes to public statements. What they said last year was simply insane. In a way, they've already thrown TCR under the bus by saying that if Bloodlines 3 will ever get made, it won't be TCR. They said that last year - before the release. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}